": "7_6", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Solve \\"Rising Temperature\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/rising-temperature/"}, {"id": "pg-7-prob-7", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/biggest-single-number/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/biggest-single-number/", "name": "Biggest Single Number", "title": "Biggest Single Number", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "7_7", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Solve \\"Biggest Single Number\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/biggest-single-number/"}, {"id": "pg-7-prob-8", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/actors-and-directors-who-cooperated-at-least-three-times/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/actors-and-directors-who-cooperated-at-least-three-times/", "name": "Actors and Directors Who Cooperated At Least Three Times", "title": "Actors and Directors Who Cooperated At Least Three Times", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "7_8", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Solve \\"Actors and Directors Who Cooperated At Least Three Times\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/actors-and-directors-who-cooperated-at-least-three-times/"}, {"id": "pg-7-prob-9", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/recyclable-and-low-fat-products/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/recyclable-and-low-fat-products/", "name": "Recyclable and Low Fat Products", "title": "Recyclable and Low Fat Products", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "7_9", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Solve \\"Recyclable and Low Fat Products\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/recyclable-and-low-fat-products/"}, {"id": "pg-7-prob-10", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/find-customer-referee/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/find-customer-referee/", "name": "Find Customer Referee", "title": "Find Customer Referee", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "7_10", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Solve \\"Find Customer Referee\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/find-customer-referee/"}]	\N	### 📌 Topic Overview\nRemoving data in production systems requires choosing between three distinct strategies: **Soft Delete** (archiving via a boolean flag), **Hard `DELETE`** (row-by-row removal), and **`TRUNCATE`** (instant table-wide page deallocation).\n\n### ⚖️ Soft Delete vs. Hard `DELETE` vs. `TRUNCATE`\n\n* **Soft Delete:** `UPDATE users SET is_active = false WHERE ...` — Fast — Preserves historical payments, invoices, and audit logs while hiding the user from the UI.\n* **Hard `DELETE`:** `DELETE FROM users WHERE ...` — Slower on large sets (scans & logs row-by-row) — Permanently removing specific spam accounts or filtered records.\n* **`TRUNCATE`:** `TRUNCATE TABLE users;` — Instant (deallocates data pages at once) — Wiping an entire staging/test table clean without dropping its schema.\n\n### 💻 Core SQL Syntax & Patterns\n\n```sql\n-- 1. Soft Delete (Recommended for production user accounts)\nUPDATE users\nSET is_active = false\nWHERE email = 'aakash.basnet@college.com';\n\n-- 2. Single-Row Hard Delete with RETURNING confirmation\nDELETE FROM users\nWHERE email = 'spam@bot.com'\nRETURNING id, name, email;\n\n-- 3. Batch Hard Delete (Remove all inactive accounts)\nDELETE FROM users\nWHERE is_active = false;\n\n-- 4. Instant Table Wipe + Reset SERIAL Counter back to 1\nTRUNCATE TABLE users RESTART IDENTITY;\n```	Thapa Technical (Vinod Bahadur Thapa)	https://www.youtube.com/@ThapaTechnical	654	Lecture 7: Deleting Data Safely — DELETE vs. TRUNCATE, Soft Deletes & RESTART IDENTITY	Compare row-by-row DELETE against page-level TRUNCATE, implement non-destructive Soft Deletes for audit trails, and reset sequences with RESTART IDENTITY.	14	Easy	Module 2: CRUD Operations & Data Manipulation	7	[{"id": "pg-7-prob-1", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/delete-dupl