s/restaurant-growth/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/restaurant-growth/", "name": "Restaurant Growth", "title": "Restaurant Growth", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "10_9", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Solve \\"Restaurant Growth\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/restaurant-growth/"}, {"id": "pg-10-prob-10", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/classes-more-than-5-students/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/classes-more-than-5-students/", "name": "Classes More Than 5 Students", "title": "Classes More Than 5 Students", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "10_10", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Solve \\"Classes More Than 5 Students\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/classes-more-than-5-students/"}]	\N	### 📌 Topic Overview\nEvery e-commerce catalog and admin dashboard relies on **Sorting** (`ORDER BY`) and **Pagination** (`LIMIT` + `OFFSET`) to deliver data in predictable, bite-sized pages.\n\n### 🗂️ 1. Single & Multi-Column Sorting (`ORDER BY`)\n* **`ASC` (Ascending):** Lowest to highest / A to Z *(Default if omitted)*.\n* **`DESC` (Descending):** Highest to lowest / Z to A.\n\n```sql\n-- Top 3 Most Expensive Courses\nSELECT title, fee\nFROM courses\nORDER BY fee DESC\nLIMIT 3;\n\n-- Multi-Column Sorting: Group by role (admin, professor, student), then sort names A-Z within each role\nSELECT role, name\nFROM users\nORDER BY role ASC, name ASC;\n```\n\n### 📄 2. Offset-Based API Pagination (`LIMIT` + `OFFSET`)\nFor a page size of `10` records per page, the formula for `OFFSET` on page $P$ is `(P - 1) * 10`:\n\n```sql\n-- Page 1 (Rows 1 to 10)\nSELECT id, name, email FROM users ORDER BY id ASC LIMIT 10 OFFSET 0;\n\n-- Page 2 (Skip first 10 -> Rows 11 to 20)\nSELECT id, name, email FROM users ORDER BY id ASC LIMIT 10 OFFSET 10;\n\n-- Page 3 (Skip first 20 -> Rows 21 to 30)\nSELECT id, name, email FROM users ORDER BY id ASC LIMIT 10 OFFSET 20;\n```\n\n### 💡 3 High-Frequency Backend Interview Insights\n1. **Never Use `LIMIT` Without `ORDER BY`:** Without `ORDER BY`, PostgreSQL returns rows in whatever physical heap order they sit on disk, which changes unpredictably as rows are updated.\n2. **The `NULLS LAST` Trick:** PostgreSQL treats `NULL` as larger than any non-null value. In `ORDER BY price DESC`, products with `price IS NULL` appear at the very top! Fix this with:\n   ```sql\n   SELECT title, fee FROM courses ORDER BY fee DESC NULLS LAST;\n   ```\n3. **Why Deep `OFFSET` Is Slow at Scale:** `OFFSET 1000000` forces PostgreSQL to scan and discard 1,000,000 rows before returning 10. For massive tables, use **Cursor/Keyset Pagination** (`WHERE id > last_seen_id ORDER BY id ASC LIMIT 10`).	Thapa Technical (Vinod Bahadur Thapa)	https://www.youtube.com/@ThapaTechnical	654	Lecture 10: Sorting & Pagination — ORDER BY, Multi-Column Sorting, LIMIT, OFFSET & NULLS LAST	Sort query results with ORDER BY ASC/DESC, implement multi-column sorting, build paginated APIs with LIMIT and OFFSET, and handle NULL sorting edge cases.	20	Easy	Module 3: Filtering, Pattern Matching & Pagination	10	[{"id": "pg-10-prob-1", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/second-highest-salary/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/second-highest-salary/", "name": "Second Highest Salary (ORDER BY DESC + LIMIT + OFFSET)", "title": "Second Highest Salary (ORDER BY DESC + LIMIT + OFFSET)", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "10_1", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Solve \\"Second Highest Salary (ORDER BY DESC + LIMIT + OFFSET)\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/second-highest-salary/"}, {"id": "pg-10-prob-2", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/nth-highest-salary/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/nth-highest-salary/", "name": "Nth Highest Salary (Dynamic OFFSET Pagination)", "title": "Nth Highest Salary (Dynamic OFFSET Pagination)", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "10_