4", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Users and servers are distributed across different timezones (e.g., a server in US-East serving users in India at UTC+5:30 and London at UTC+0). Storing UTC timestamps (like 2025-10-18T14:00:00Z or Date.now() epoch milliseconds) provides a single unambiguous point in time. When sent to the browser, the client's Date object automatically renders that UTC timestamp in the user's local OS timezone."}, {"id": "js-lec-6-q5", "url": null, "link": null, "name": "Q5: What is the difference between str.replace() and str.replaceAll()?", "title": "Q5: What is the difference between str.replace() and str.replaceAll()?", "answer": "When passed a string pattern, str.replace(\\"a\\", \\"b\\") replaces ONLY the very first occurrence of \\"a\\" (unless a global regex /a/g is used). str.replaceAll(\\"a\\", \\"b\\") (introduced in ES2021) replaces every occurrence of the substring across the entire string without requiring a regular expression.", "platform": "Technical Interview QA", "problemId": "6-q5", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "When passed a string pattern, str.replace(\\"a\\", \\"b\\") replaces ONLY the very first occurrence of \\"a\\" (unless a global regex /a/g is used). str.replaceAll(\\"a\\", \\"b\\") (introduced in ES2021) replaces every occurrence of the substring across the entire string without requiring a regular expression."}, {"id": "js-lec-6-q6", "url": null, "link": null, "name": "Q6: How do you calculate the exact number of days, hours, minutes, and seconds remaining for a countdown timer between now and a target future date?", "title": "Q6: How do you calculate the exact number of days, hours, minutes, and seconds remaining for a countdown timer between now and a target future date?", "answer": "Subtract the current millisecond timestamp from the target millisecond timestamp: const diffMs = targetDate.getTime() - Date.now(). Then compute: days = Math.floor(diffMs / (1000 * 60 * 60 * 24)), hours = Math.floor((diffMs / (1000 * 60 * 60)) % 24), minutes = Math.floor((diffMs / (1000 * 60)) % 60), and seconds = Math.floor((diffMs / 1000) % 60).", "platform": "Technical Interview QA", "problemId": "6-q6", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Subtract the current millisecond timestamp from the target millisecond timestamp: const diffMs = targetDate.getTime() - Date.now(). Then compute: days = Math.floor(diffMs / (1000 * 60 * 60 * 24)), hours = Math.floor((diffMs / (1000 * 60 * 60)) % 24), minutes = Math.floor((diffMs / (1000 * 60)) % 60), and seconds = Math.floor((diffMs / 1000) % 60)."}]	https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/String	\N	\N	\N
