", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Return inventory where **quantity** is greater than 50.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bf7a3fe74e0db37639"}, {"id": "mongo-11-prob-10", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bd7a3fe74e0db375a3", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bd7a3fe74e0db375a3", "name": "Problem #164: Find articles with views lt 500", "title": "Problem #164: Find articles with views lt 500", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "164", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Return articles where **views** < 500.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bd7a3fe74e0db375a3"}, {"id": "mongo-11-prob-11", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bd7a3fe74e0db375a0", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bd7a3fe74e0db375a0", "name": "Problem #165: Find articles with views gt 2000", "title": "Problem #165: Find articles with views gt 2000", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "165", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Return articles where **views** > 2000.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bd7a3fe74e0db375a0"}, {"id": "mongo-11-prob-12", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bd7a3fe74e0db3759d", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bd7a3fe74e0db3759d", "name": "Problem #166: Find logs with level in info warn", "title": "Problem #166: Find logs with level in info warn", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "166", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Return logs where **level** is info or warn.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bd7a3fe74e0db3759d"}]	\N	### 📌 Topic Overview\nMongoDB **Comparison Query Operators** allow you to filter documents by numeric ranges, inequalities, and set memberships inside `find()`, `updateOne()` / `updateMany()`, and `deleteOne()` / `deleteMany()`.\n\n### 💡 All 8 Comparison Operators\nEvery comparison operator is placed inside a nested object attached to the target field: `{ <field>: { <$operator>: <value> } }`.\n* **`$eq` (Equal To):** Matches values strictly equal to the target value (`{ age: { $eq: 20 } }` is equivalent to `{ age: 20 }`).\n* **`$ne` (Not Equal To):** Matches all documents where the field value does NOT equal the target value (`{ class: { $ne: "BCA" } }`).\n* **`$gt` (Greater Than):** Matches numeric or date values strictly greater than the target (`{ age: { $gt: 20 } }` -> 21, 22, 23...).\n* **`$gte` (Greater Than or Equal To):** Matches values greater than or equal to the target (`{ age: { $gte: 20 } }` -> 20, 21, 22...).\n* **`$lt` (Less Than):** Matches values strictly less than the target (`{ age: { $lt: 20 } }` -> 19, 18...).\n* **`$lte` (Less Than or Equal To):** Matches values less than or equal to the target (`{ age: { $lte: 20 } }` -> 20, 19...).\n* **`$in` (In Array):** Matches documents where the field value equals **any** value in the provided array (`{ class: { $in: ["BCA", "BSc" } }` — cleaner alternative to multiple OR conditions).\n* **`$nin` (Not In Array):** Matches documents where the field value does **not** match any value in the array (`{ age: { $nin: [20, 24 } }`).\n\n### 🛠️ Practical Comparison Queries in find(), updateMany() & deleteMany()\n```javascript\n// 1. Range & Inequality Queries in find()\ndb.students.find({ age: { $gt: 20 } })\ndb.students.find({ age: { $lte: 20 } })\ndb.students.find({ class: { $ne: "BCA" } })\n\n// 2. Matching Multiple Values with $in and $nin\ndb.students.find({ age: { $in: [20, 24 } })\ndb.students.find({ class: { $in: ["BCA", "BSc" } })\ndb.students.find({ class: { $nin: ["BCA", "BSc" } })\n\n// 3. Using Comparison Operators inside updateMany()\n// Promote all students younger than 20 to class "12th"\ndb.students.updateMany(\n  { age: { $lt: 20 } },\n  { $set: { class: "12th" } }\n)\n\n// 4. Using Comparison Operators inside deleteMany()\n// Delete all students younger than 20\ndb.students.deleteMany({ age: { $lt: 20 } })\n```	Yahoo Baba	https://www.youtube.com/@YahooBaba	655	Lecture 11: Comparison Query Operators — $eq, $ne, $gt, $gte, $lt, $lte, $in & $nin	Write expressive filter queries across find(), updateMany(), and deleteMany() using MongoDB comparison operators: $eq, $ne, $gt, $gte, $lt, $lte, $in, and $nin.	20	Easy	\N	11	[{"id": "mongo-11-prob-1", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9c17a3fe74e0db3771b", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9c17a3fe74e0db3771b", "name": "Problem #40: Reviews with rating lt 3", "title": "Problem #40: Reviews with rating lt 3", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "40", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Return reviews where rating < 3.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9c17a3fe74e0db3771b"}, {"id": "mongo-11-prob-2", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9c17a3fe74e0db37718", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9c17a3fe74e0db37718", "name": "Problem #41: Reviews with rating gte 4", "title": "Problem #41: Reviews with rating gte 4", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "41", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Return reviews where rating >= 4.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9c17a3fe74e0db37718"}, {"id": "mongo-11-prob-3", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9c17a3fe74e0db37715", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9c17a3fe74e0db37715", "name": "Problem #42: Inventory with quantity lte 60", "title": "Problem #42: Inventory with quantity lte 60", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "42", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Return inventory wh