seRef`?", "explanation": "By passing the ref object to the `ref` attribute of an element, React automatically assigns the actual DOM node to `ref.current`.", "correctAnswer": "A", "correct_index": 0, "correct_answer": "Pass the ref object to the `ref` attribute of a JSX element"}, {"id": 3, "type": "multiple_choice", "answer": "B", "options": ["No, it is strictly for DOM access", "Yes, it acts like an instance variable that persists data without causing re-renders", "Yes, but it resets on every state change", "No, the value resets if the component re-renders"], "question": "Can `useRef` be used to store mutable values across renders?", "explanation": "useRef provides a persistent memory container across the full lifecycle of the component without interfering with the render cycle.", "correctAnswer": "B", "correct_index": 1, "correct_answer": "Yes, it acts like an instance variable that persists data without causing re-renders"}]	\N	> **Architectural Deep Dive:** This lecture covers the strict technical nuances, reconciliation behavior, and performance implications of using useRef in production environments. Pay special attention to concurrent rendering behaviors in React 18+.	Web Dev Simplified	https://www.youtube.com/@WebDevSimplified	\N	Learn useRef in 11 Minutes	Deep dive architectural lecture focusing on the mechanics, use cases, and anti-patterns of the useRef hook.	11	Easy	Core Hooks & API	4	[]	\N	11	https://youtu.be/t2ypzz6gJm0	Learn useRef in 11 Minutes
22093	Lecture 8: Updating & Replacing Documents — updateOne, updateMany, Field & Array Update Operators	mongo-lecture-8-update-replace-documents-field-array-operators	Modify documents using updateOne(), updateMany(), and replaceOne() with field operators ($set, $unset, $rename, $inc, $mul, $min, $max, $currentDate) and array operators ($push, $addToSet, $pop, $pull, $pullAll).	2026-10-06 19:11:34.825286+05:30	### 📌 Topic Overview\nMongoDB provides three core methods to modify existing documents: **`updateOne(filter, update)`** (updates the first matching document), **`updateMany(filter, update)`** (updates all matching documents), and **`replaceOne(filter, replacement)`** (replaces the entire document while keeping its `_id`).\n\n### 💡 Field Update Operators\n* **`$set`:** Updates the value of existing fields or adds new fields if they do not exist.\n* **`$unset`:** Completely removes a field from the document (e.g., `{ $unset: { age: "" } }`).\n* **`$rename`:** Renames a field key without altering its value (e.g., `{ $rename: { "skills": "coding_skills" } }`).\n* **`$inc`:** Increments (or decrements with a negative number) a numeric field by a specified amount (e.g., `{ $inc: { age: 2 } }`).\n* **`$mul`:** Multiplies a numeric field by a factor (e.g., `{ $mul: { age: 2 } }`).\n* **`$min`:** Updates the field ONLY if the specified value is **less than** the existing field value.\n* **`$max`:** Updates the field ONLY if the specified value is **greater than** the existing field value.\n* **`$currentDate`:** Sets a field to the current UTC date/timestamp (e.g., `{ $currentDate: { lastModified: true } }`).\n\n### 💡 Array Update Operators\n* **`$push`:** Appends a new value to the end of an array (allows duplicates).\n* **`$addToSet`:** Appends a value to an array **only if it does not already exist** in the array (prevents duplicates).\n* **`$pop`:** Removes the **last** element of an array when passed `1` (`{ $pop: { skills: 1 } }`) or the **first** element when passed `-1` (`{ $pop: { skills: -1 } }`).\n* **`$pull`:** Removes all occurrences of a specific matching value from anywhere in an array (e.g., `{ $pull: { skills: "Python" } }`).\n* **`$pullAll`:** Removes multiple specified values from an array at once (e.g., `{ $pullAll: { skills: ["HTML", "JavaScript" } }`).\n\n### 🛠️ Practical Update & Replace Examples\n```javascript\n// 1. Update fields on a single document with $set and $inc\ndb.students.updateOne(\n  { _id: ObjectId("671398e3d620709480d144bd") },\n  {\n    $set: { class: "BTech" },\n    $inc: { age: 2 }\n  }\n)\n\n// 2. Bulk update all BCA students to BIT & stamp lastModified date\ndb.students.updateMany(\n  { class: "BCA" },\n  {\n    $set: { class: "BIT" },\n    $currentDate: { lastModified: true }\n  }\n)\n\n// 3. Array modifications: $addToSet (unique append) and $pullAll\ndb.students.updateOne(\n  { name: "Salman Khan" },\n  { $addToSet: { skills: "Java" } }\n)\n\ndb.students.updateOne(\n  { name: "John Abraham" },\n  { $pullAll: { skills: ["JavaScript", "HTML" } }\n)\n\n// 4. Replace an entire document while preserving its _id\ndb.students.replaceOne(\n  { name: "Shahid Kapoor" },\n  {\n    name: "Saif Ali Khan",\n    age: 21,\n    skills: ["Go", "C++"\n  }\n)\n```	[{"url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/update/", "link": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/update/", "title": "MongoDB Official Manual — Lecture 8: Updating & Replacing Documents"}]	[{"url": "http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Aox_DHFnqTg", "title": "MongoDB Update & Replace Documents Tutorial in Hindi / Urdu", "duration": "34m", "creator_name": "Yahoo Baba", "creator_channel_url": "https://www.youtube.com/@YahooBaba"}]	[{"id": "mongo-8-prob-1", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bd7a3fe74e0db37594", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bd7a3fe74e0db37594", "name": "Problem #169: Articles with tags size 4", "title": "Problem #169: Articles with tags size 4", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "169", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Return articles that have exactly 4 tags.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bd7a3fe74e0db37594"}, {"id": "mongo-8-prob-2", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bb7a3fe74e0db374bd", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bb7a3fe74e0db374bd", "name": "Problem #240: Orders with items qty greater than 1", "title": "Problem #240: Orders with items qty greater than 1", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "240", "difficulty": "Hard", "description": "Return orders where at least one item has **qty** > 1. Use **$elemMatch** on items.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bb7a3fe74e0db374bd"}, {"id": "mongo-8-prob-3", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b77a3fe74e0db37348", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b77a3fe74e0db37348", "name": "Problem #361: Orders with items array length 3", "title": "Problem #361: Orders with items array length 3", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "361", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Return orders that have exactly 3 elements in **items**. Use **$size**.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b77a3fe74e0db37348"}, {"id": "mongo-8-prob-4", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b77a3fe74e0db37345", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b77a3fe74e0db37345", "name": "Problem #362: ElemMatch ratings all greater than 3", "title": "Problem #362: ElemMatch ratings all greater than 3", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "362", "difficulty": "Hard", "description": "Return products where at least one element in **ratings** is greater than 3. Use **$elemMatch**.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b77a3fe74e0db37345"}, {"id": "mongo-8-prob-5", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b77a3fe74e0db37342", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b77a3fe74e0db37342", "name": "Problem #363: Find products with rating 5 in ratings", "title": "Problem #363: Find products with rating 5 in ratings", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "363", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Return products that have 5 in their **ratings** array.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b77a3fe74e0db37342"}, {"id": "mongo-8-prob-6", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b77a3fe74e0db37327", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b77a3fe74e0db37327", "name": "Problem #372: Products with attribute color red", "title": "Problem #372: Products with attribute color red", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "372", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Return products where **attributes.color** is \\"red\\". Use dot notation.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b77a3fe74e0db37327"}, {"id": "mongo-8-prob-7", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b77a3fe74e0db37318", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b77a3fe74e0db37318", "name": "Problem #377: Find orders with exactly 2 items", "title": "Problem #377: Find orders with exactly 2 items", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "377", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Return orders where **items** array has exactly 2 elements. Use **$size**.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b77a3fe74e0db37318"}, {"id": "mongo-8-prob-8", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b67a3fe74e0db37303", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b67a3fe74e0db37303", "name": "Problem #384: Products with ratings array size 3", "title": "Problem #384: Products with ratings array size 3", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "384", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Return products whose **ratings** array has exactly 3 elements. Use **$size**.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b67a3fe74e0db37303"}, {"id": "mongo-8-prob-9", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b47a3fe74e0db371fb", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b47a3fe74e0db371fb", "name": "Problem #462: Find users with both tag1 and tag2", "title": "Problem #462: Find users with both tag1 and tag2", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "462", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Return users whose **tags** array contains both \\"tag1\\" and \\"tag2\\". Use **$all**.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b47a3fe74e0db371fb"}, {"id": "mongo-8-prob-10", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b47a3fe74e0db371ec", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b47a3fe74e0db371ec", "name": "Problem #467: Find users with tags array size 1", "title": "Problem #467: Find users with tags array size 1", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "467", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Return users that have exactly 1 element in **tags**. Use **$size**.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b47a3fe74e0db371ec"}, {"id": "mongo-8-prob-11", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b37a3fe74e0db371c2", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b37a3fe74e0db371c2", "name": "Problem #481: Find users with tag2 in tags", "title": "Problem #481: Find users with tag2 in tags", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "481", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Return users that have \\"tag2\\" in their **tags** array.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b37a3fe74e0db371c2"}, {"id": "mongo-8-prob-12", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b37a3fe74e0db371aa", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b37a3fe74e0db371aa", "name": "Problem #489: Find users with exactly two tags", "title": "Problem #489: Find users with exactly two tags", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "489", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Return users whose **tags** array has exactly 2 elements. Use **$size**.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b37a3fe74e0db371aa"}]	\N	### 📌 Topic Overview\nMongoDB provides three core methods to modify existing documents: **`updateOne(filter, update)`** (updates the first matching document), **`updateMany(filter, update)`** (updates all matching documents), and **`replaceOne(filter, replacement)`** (replaces the entire document while keeping its `_id`).\n\n### 💡 Field Update Operators\n* **`$set`:** Updates the value of existing fields or adds new fields if they do not exist.\n* **`$unset`:** Completely removes a field from the document (e.g., `{ $unset: { age: "" } }`).\n* **`$rename`:** Renames a field key without altering its value (e.g., `{ $rename: { "skills": "coding_skills" } }`).\n* **`$inc`:** Increments (or decrements with a negative number) a numeric field by a specified amount (e.g., `{ $inc: { age: 2 } }`).\n* **`$mul`:** Multiplies a numeric field by a factor (e.g., `{ $mul: { age: 2 } }`).\n* **`$min`:** Updates the field ONLY if the specified value is **less than** the existing field value.\n* **`$max`:** Updates the field ONLY if the specified value is **greater than** the existing field value.\n* **`$currentDate`:** Sets a field to the current UTC date/timestamp (e.g., `{ $currentDate: { lastModified: true } }`).\n\n### 💡 Array Update Operators\n* **`$push`:** Appends a new value to the end of an array (allows duplicates).\n* **`$addToSet`:** Appends a value to an array **only if it does not already exist** in the array (prevents duplicates).\n* **`$pop`:** Removes the **last** element of an array when passed `1` (`{ $pop: { skills: 1 } }`) or the **first** element when passed `-1` (`{ $pop: { skills: -1 } }`).\n* **`$pull`:** Removes all occurrences of a specific matching value from anywhere in an array (e.g., `{ $pull: { skills: "Python" } }`).\n* **`$pullAll`:** Removes multiple specified values from an array at once (e.g., `{ $pullAll: { skills: ["HTML", "JavaScript" } }`).\n\n### 🛠️ Practical Update & Replace Examples\n```javascript\n// 1. Update fields on a single document with $set and $inc\ndb.students.updateOne(\n  { _id: ObjectId("671398e3d620709480d144bd") },\n  {\n    $set: { class: "BTech" },\n    $inc: { age: 2 }\n  }\n)\n\n// 2. Bulk update all BCA students to BIT & stamp lastModified date\ndb.students.updateMany(\n  { class: "BCA" },\n  {\n    $set: { class: "BIT" },\n    $currentDate: { lastModified: true }\n  }\n)\n\n// 3. Array modifications: $addToSet (unique append) and $pullAll\ndb.students.updateOne(\n  { name: "Salman Khan" },\n  { $addToSet: { skills: "Java" } }\n)\n\ndb.students.updateOne(\n  { name: "John Abraham" },\n  { $pullAll: { skills: ["JavaScript", "HTML" } }\n)\n\n// 4. Replace an entire document while preserving its _id\ndb.students.replaceOne(\n  { name: "Shahid Kapoor" },\n  {\n    name: "Saif Ali Khan",\n    age: 21,\n    skills: ["Go", "C++"\n  }\n)\n```	Yahoo Baba	https://www.youtube.com/@YahooBaba	655	Lecture 8: Updating & Replacing Documents — updateOne, updateMany, Field & Array Update Operators	Modify documents using updateOne(), updateMany(), and replaceOne() with field operators ($set, $unset, $rename, $inc, $mul, $min, $max, $currentDate) and array operators ($push, $addToSet, $pop, $pull, $pullAll).