oblemId": "14_5", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Solve \\"Actors and Directors Who Cooperated At Least Three Times\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/actors-and-directors-who-cooperated-at-least-three-times/"}, {"id": "pg-14-prob-6", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/article-views-i/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/article-views-i/", "name": "Article Views I", "title": "Article Views I", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "14_6", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Solve \\"Article Views I\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/article-views-i/"}, {"id": "pg-14-prob-7", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/employee-bonus/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/employee-bonus/", "name": "Employee Bonus", "title": "Employee Bonus", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "14_7", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Solve \\"Employee Bonus\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/employee-bonus/"}, {"id": "pg-14-prob-8", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/managers-with-at-least-5-direct-reports/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/managers-with-at-least-5-direct-reports/", "name": "Managers with at Least 5 Direct Reports", "title": "Managers with at Least 5 Direct Reports", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "14_8", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Solve \\"Managers with at Least 5 Direct Reports\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/managers-with-at-least-5-direct-reports/"}, {"id": "pg-14-prob-9", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/recyclable-and-low-fat-products/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/recyclable-and-low-fat-products/", "name": "Recyclable and Low Fat Products", "title": "Recyclable and Low Fat Products", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "14_9", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Solve \\"Recyclable and Low Fat Products\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/recyclable-and-low-fat-products/"}, {"id": "pg-14-prob-10", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/find-customer-referee/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/find-customer-referee/", "name": "Find Customer Referee", "title": "Find Customer Referee", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "14_10", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Solve \\"Find Customer Referee\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/find-customer-referee/"}]	\N	### 📌 Topic Overview\nThis hands-on session implements the **`enrollments` Junction Table** connecting `users` and `courses`, demonstrates how PostgreSQL blocks invalid "ghost" Foreign Key inserts, and shows how to retrofit a Foreign Key onto an already-created table (`library_books`).\n\n### 🛠️ 1. Creating the `enrollments` Junction Table\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE enrollments (\n    id BIGSERIAL PRIMARY KEY,\n    student_id INT REFERENCES users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n    course_id INT REFERENCES courses(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n    enrolled_on DATE DEFAULT CURRENT_DATE\n);\n\n-- Valid Enrollment Insert (User #9 into Course #3)\nINSERT INTO enrollments (student_id, course_id)\nVALUES (9, 3)\nRETURNING *;\n```\n\n### 🛡️ 2. Referential Integrity in Action (Blocking Ghost Records)\nAttempting to enroll a student into a non-existent course (`course_id = 9999`) is immediately rejected by the storage engine:\n```sql\n-- ❌ Throws: ERROR: insert or update on table "enrollments" violates foreign key constraint\n-- Detail: Key (course_id)=(9999) is not present in table "courses".\nINSERT INTO enrollments (student_id, course_id)\nVALUES (9, 9999);\n```\n\n### 🔧 3. Retrofitting a Foreign Key to an Existing Table (`ALTER TABLE`)\nIf you created a table (`library_books`) with an integer column (`borrowed_by_user_id`) but forgot to attach the `REFERENCES` constraint during creation, add a named Foreign Key constraint using `ALTER TABLE`:\n\n```sql\n-- Table created without FK constraint initially\nCREATE TABLE library_books (\n    id SERIAL PRIMARY KEY,\n    title VARCHAR(150) NOT NULL,\n    borrowed_by_user_id INT,\n    borrowed_on DATE DEFAULT CURRENT_DATE\n);\n\n-- Retrofit named Foreign Key constraint onto the existing table\nALTER TABLE library_books\nADD CONSTRAINT fk_borrowed_by_user\nFOREIGN KEY (borrowed_by_user_id)\nREFERENCES users(id)\nON DELETE SET NULL;\n```	Thapa Technical (Vinod Bahadur Thapa)	https://www.youtube.com/@ThapaTechnical	654	Lecture 14: Foreign Keys in Action — Building Junction Tables, Referential Integrity & ALTER TABLE FK	Practically implement the enrollments junction table, test Foreign Key constraint violations against ghost IDs, and retrofit Foreign Keys onto existing tables.	16	Medium	Module 4: Schema Integrity, Keys & Relationships	14	[{"id": "pg-14-prob-1", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/combine-two-tables/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/combine-two-tables/", "name": "Combine Two Tables (Relational PK/FK Lookup)", "title": "Combine Two Tables (Relational PK/FK Lookup)", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "14_1", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Solve \\"Combine Two Tables (Relational PK/FK Lookup)\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/combine-two-tables/"}, {"id": "pg-14-prob-2", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/customers-who-never-order/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/customers-who-never-order/", "name": "Customers Who Never Order (Unmatched Foreign Keys)", "title": "Customers Who Never Order (Unmatched Foreign Keys)", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "14_2", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Solve \\"Customers Who Never Order (Unmatched Foreign Keys)\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/customers-who-never-order/"}, {"id": "pg-14-prob-3", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/employees-earning-more-than-their-managers/", "link"