e entire Home object inside favourite.json and the host later updated the home's price or photo in homes.json, the copy inside favourite.json would become stale and out-of-sync! Storing only the homeId reference ensures that when we look up favourites against Home.fetchAll(), users always see the latest updated home details."}, {"id": "node-lec-14-q3", "url": null, "link": null, "name": "Q3: What is the data type of req.params.homeId when a user visits /homes/42, and what bug can happen if home.id is stored as a Number?", "title": "Q3: What is the data type of req.params.homeId when a user visits /homes/42, and what bug can happen if home.id is stored as a Number?", "answer": "Every value inside req.params is ALWAYS a String (so req.params.homeId is \\"42\\"). If home.id was stored as a numeric 42, strict equality home.id === req.params.homeId (42 === \\"42\\") will evaluate to false! Always ensure consistent types (either store IDs as strings or convert via Number(req.params.homeId) / String(home.id)).", "platform": "Technical Interview QA", "problemId": "14-q3", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Every value inside req.params is ALWAYS a String (so req.params.homeId is \\"42\\"). If home.id was stored as a numeric 42, strict equality home.id === req.params.homeId (42 === \\"42\\") will evaluate to false! Always ensure consistent types (either store IDs as strings or convert via Number(req.params.homeId) / String(home.id))."}, {"id": "node-lec-14-q4", "url": null, "link": null, "name": "Q4: How do you pass a home.id from an EJS card button when submitting a POST \\"/favourites\\" request without putting the ID in the URL?", "title": "Q4: How do you pass a home.id from an EJS card button when submitting a POST \\"/favourites\\" request without putting the ID in the URL?", "answer": "Place a hidden input field inside the <form action=\\"/favourites\\" method=\\"POST\\">: <input type=\\"hidden\\" name=\\"id\\" value=\\"<%= home.id %>\\" />. When the user clicks the Submit button, the browser sends id in the POST request body (req.body.id) without displaying the input box on the UI.", "platform": "Technical Interview QA", "problemId": "14-q4", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Place a hidden input field inside the <form action=\\"/favourites\\" method=\\"POST\\">: <input type=\\"hidden\\" name=\\"id\\" value=\\"<%= home.id %>\\" />. When the user clicks the Submit button, the browser sends id in the POST request body (req.body.id) without displaying the input box on the UI."}, {"id": "node-lec-14-q5", "url": null, "link": null, "name": "Q5: What should a controller do if Home.findById(req.params.homeId) returns undefined (e.g., a user typed a non-existent or deleted ID in the URL)?", "title": "Q5: What should a controller do if Home.findById(req.params.homeId) returns undefined (e.g., a user typed a non-existent or deleted ID in the URL)?", "answer": "If you pass home: undefined directly into res.render(\\"store/home-detail\\", { home }), the EJS template will crash with TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'houseName'). Always guard with if (!home) return res.redirect(\\"/homes\\") (or render a 404 page) before calling res.render().", "platform": "Technical Interview QA", "problemId": "14-q5", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "If you pass home: undefined directly into res.render(\\"store/home-detail\\", { home }), the EJS template will crash with TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'houseName'). Always guard with if (!home) return res.redirect(\\"/homes\\") (or render a 404 page) before calling res.render()."}, {"id": "node-lec-14-q6", "url": null, "link": null, "name": "Q6: Can a single Express route have multiple route parameters (e.g., /users/:userId/bookings/:bookingId)?", "title": "Q6: Can a single Express route have multiple route parameters (e.g., /users/:userId/bookings/:bookingId)?", "answer": "Yes! Express supports multiple route parameters in the same path pattern. A r