22115	Lecture 30: Indexing & Query Optimization — COLLSCAN vs. IXSCAN, explain("executionStats"), Single, Compound, Unique, Text & Wildcard Indexes	mongo-lecture-30-indexes-explain-executionstats-compound-unique-text-wildcard	Eliminate slow collection scans (COLLSCAN) using B-Tree indexes (IXSCAN), analyze query plans with explain("executionStats"), and master Single-Field, Compound, Unique, Text, Wildcard ($**), and Multikey Array indexes.	2026-10-06 19:52:12.616986+05:30	### 📌 Topic Overview\nWithout an index, MongoDB must perform a **Collection Scan (`COLLSCAN`)**, inspecting every single document in the collection to find matches. Creating an **Index** builds an in-memory B-Tree lookup structure so MongoDB jumps directly to matching records via an **Index Scan (`IXSCAN` / `EXPRESS_IXSCAN`)**.\n\n### 💡 Analyzing Query Performance & Managing Indexes\n* **`.explain("executionStats")`:** Appended to any `find()` query to inspect the query planner stage (`COLLSCAN` vs. `IXSCAN`), `totalDocsExamined`, and execution time in milliseconds.\n* **`db.<collection>.createIndex({ <field>: 1 | -1 }, <options>)`:** Creates an ascending (`1`) or descending (`-1`) index.\n* **`db.<collection>.getIndexes()`:** Lists all active indexes on the collection (note that `_id_1` is created automatically by MongoDB on every collection).\n* **`db.<collection>.dropIndex("<index_name>")`:** Deletes a specific index by its name (e.g., `"name_-1"`).\n\n### 💡 Complete Index Types Covered\n* **1. Single-Field Index:** Indexes a single frequently queried field: `createIndex({ name: -1 })`.\n* **2. Compound Index:** Indexes multiple fields together in a specific sort order: `createIndex({ class: 1, age: -1 })`. Accelerates queries filtering on `class` and sorting by `age`.\n* **3. Unique Index:** Enforces uniqueness across a field so duplicate values (such as duplicate `email` addresses) are rejected with `E11000 duplicate key error`: `createIndex({ email: 1 }, { unique: true })`.\n* **4. Text Index:** Tokenizes string/paragraph fields for fast full-text word search:\n  * Create: `createIndex({ name: "text" })`\n  * Query: `find({ $text: { $search: "Khan" } })`\n* **5. Wildcard Index (`$**`):** Automatically indexes **all fields** across every document: `createIndex({ "$**": 1 })`. Useful for unpredictable schemas, though it consumes significantly more RAM.\n* **6. Multikey Index (Array Field Index):** Calling `createIndex({ skills: 1 })` on an array field automatically indexes every individual element inside the array.\n\n### 🛠️ Practical Indexing & Query Plan Analysis\n```javascript\n// 1. Inspect query execution plan BEFORE and AFTER indexing\ndb.students.find({ name: "Aamir Khan" }).explain("executionStats")\n// Before index: stage = "COLLSCAN", totalDocsExamined = 7\n\ndb.students.createIndex({ name: -1 })\ndb.students.find({ name: "Aamir Khan" }).explain("executionStats")\n// After index: stage = "IXSCAN", totalDocsExamined = 1\n\n// 2. Inspect and drop an existing index\ndb.students.getIndexes()\ndb.students.dropIndex("name_-1")\n\n// 3. Compound Index (class ascending, age descending)\ndb.students.createIndex({ class: 1, age: -1 })\ndb.students.find({ class: "BCA" }).sort({ age: -1 }).explain("executionStats")\n\n// 4. Unique Index on email (prevents duplicate emails & uses EXPRESS_IXSCAN)\ndb.students.createIndex({ email: 1 }, { unique: true })\n\n// 5. Full-Text Index & $text / $search query\ndb.students.createIndex({ name: "text" })\ndb.students.find({ $text: { $search: "Khan" } })\n\n// 6. Wildcard Index across all fields & Multikey Index on an Array field\ndb.students.createIndex({ "$**": 1 })\ndb.students2.createIndex({ skills: 1 })\n```	[{"url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/indexes/", "link": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/indexes/", "title": "MongoDB Official Manual — Lecture 30: Indexing & Query Optimization"}]	[{"url": "http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eax7V8RKjkE", "title": "MongoDB Indexes Tutorial in Hindi / Urdu", "duration": "35m", "creator_name": "Yahoo Baba", "creator_channel_url": "https://www.youtube.com/@YahooBaba"}]	[{"id": "mongo-30-prob-1", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bb7a3fe74e0db374cc", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bb7a3fe74e0db374cc", "name": "Problem #235: Find logs with level error", "title": "Problem #235: Find logs with level error", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "235", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Return logs where **level** is \\"error\\".", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bb7a3fe74e0db374cc"}, {"id": "mongo-30-prob-2", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9ba7a3fe74e0db37415", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9ba7a3fe74e0db37415", "name": "Problem #294: Find product by _id 15", "title": "Problem #294: Find product by _id 15", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "294", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Return the product with _id 15.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9ba7a3fe74e0db37415"}, {"id": "mongo-30-prob-3", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b97a3fe74e0db3740f", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b97a3fe74e0db3740f", "name": "Problem #296: Find customer by _id 14", "title": "Problem #296: Find customer by _id 14", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "296", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Return the customer with _id 14.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b97a3fe74e0db3740f"}, {"id": "mongo-30-prob-4", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b77a3fe74e0db37354", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b77a3fe74e0db37354", "name": "Problem #357: Find products with inStock false", "title": "Problem #357: Find products with inStock false", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "357", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Return products where **inStock** is false.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b77a3fe74e0db37354"}, {"id": "mongo-30-prob-5", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b67a3fe74e0db37300", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b67a3fe74e0db37300", "name": "Problem #385: Find products with supplierId 1", "title": "Problem #385: Find products with supplierId 1", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "385", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Return products where **supplierId** is 1.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b67a3fe74e0db37300"}, {"id": "mongo-30-prob-6", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b67a3fe74e0db372fd", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b67a3fe74e0db372fd", "name": "Problem #386: Find orders by customerId 5", "title": "Problem #386: Find orders by customerId 5", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "386", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Return orders where **customerId** is 5.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b67a3fe74e0db372fd"}, {"id": "mongo-30-prob-7", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b67a3fe74e0db372f7", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b67a3fe74e0db372f7", "name": "Problem #388: Limit products to 10", "title": "Problem #388: Limit products to 10", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "388", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Return only 10 products.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b67a3fe74e0db372f7"}, {"id": "mongo-30-prob-8", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b67a3fe74e0db37