22097	Lecture 12: Logical Query Operators — $and, $or, $nor & $not	mongo-lecture-12-logical-query-operators-and-or-nor-not	Combine multiple filter conditions across single or multiple fields in find(), updateMany(), and deleteMany() using MongoDB logical operators: $and, $or, $nor, and $not.	2026-10-06 19:28:34.895846+05:30	### 📌 Topic Overview\nWhen a single field comparison is not enough, MongoDB **Logical Query Operators** allow you to combine multiple conditions across one or more fields inside `find()`, `updateOne()` / `updateMany()`, and `deleteOne()` / `deleteMany()`.\n\n### 💡 All 4 Logical Query Operators\n* **`$and` (Logical AND):** Joins an array of query clauses `{ $and: [ { <cond1> }, { <cond2> }  }` and returns documents that satisfy **all** conditions simultaneously (e.g., `age > 20` AND `class == "BTech"`).\n* **`$or` (Logical OR):** Joins an array of query clauses `{ $or: [ { <cond1> }, { <cond2> }  }` and returns documents that satisfy **at least one** of the conditions.\n* **`$nor` (Logical NOR):** Joins an array of query clauses `{ $nor: [ { <cond1> }, { <cond2> }  }` and returns documents that **fail all** specified conditions (the exact inverse of `$or`).\n* **`$not` (Field-Level Negation):** Inverts the effect of a single operator expression on a specific field: `{ <field>: { $not: { <$operator>: <value> } } }`. Unlike `$and`, `$or`, and `$nor`, `$not` takes a single condition object (NOT an array) and is placed inside the field key.\n\n### 🛠️ Practical Logical Operator Queries\n```javascript\n// 1. $and: Students with age strictly between 20 and 25 (21, 22, 23, 24)\ndb.students.find({\n  $and: [\n    { age: { $gt: 20 } },\n    { age: { $lt: 25 } }\n  \n}, { name: 1, age: 1, class: 1, _id: 0 })\n\n// 2. $and across different fields: Age > 20 AND Class is "BTech"\ndb.students.find({\n  $and: [\n    { age: { $gt: 20 } },\n    { class: { $eq: "BTech" } }\n  \n})\n\n// 3. $or: Students who are EITHER older than 20 OR enrolled in "BTech"\ndb.students.find({\n  $or: [\n    { age: { $gt: 20 } },\n    { class: { $eq: "BTech" } }\n  \n})\n\n// 4. $nor: Students who are NEITHER older than 20 NOR enrolled in "BTech"\ndb.students.find({\n  $nor: [\n    { age: { $gt: 20 } },\n    { class: { $eq: "BTech" } }\n  \n})\n\n// 5. $not (Field-Level): Students whose age is NOT greater than 20 (i.e. <= 20)\ndb.students.find({\n  age: { $not: { $gt: 20 } }\n})\n\n// 6. Using $and inside deleteMany()\ndb.students.deleteMany({\n  $and: [\n    { age: { $gt: 20 } },\n    { class: { $eq: "BTech" } }\n  \n})\n```\n\n### ⚠️ Common Syntax Mistakes\n* **Placing `$not` at the Top Level or Passing an Array:** `$not` must always be nested inside a field (`{ age: { $not: { $gt: 20 } } }`). Writing `{ $not: [ ...  }` at the top level throws an `unknown top level operator: $not` error.	[{"url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/query-logical/", "link": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/query-logical/", "title": "MongoDB Official Manual — Lecture 12: Logical Query Operators"}]	[{"url": "http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QXbmrRJmxNs", "title": "MongoDB Logical Operators Tutorial in Hindi / Urdu", "duration": "21m", "creator_name": "Yahoo Baba", "creator_channel_url": "https://www.youtube.com/@YahooBaba"}]	[{"id": "mongo-12-prob-1", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bf7a3fe74e0db3765d", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bf7a3fe74e0db3765d", "name": "Problem #102: Find reviews with text null or missing", "title": "Problem #102: Find reviews with text null or missing", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "102", "difficulty": "Hard", "description": "Return reviews where **text** is null or does not exist. Use **$in** [null] or **$exists** false.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bf7a3fe74e0db3765d"}, {"id": "mongo-12-prob-2", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b77a3fe74e0db37369", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b77a3fe74e0db37369", "name": "Problem #350: Or: orders status delivered or cancelled", "title": "Problem #350: Or: orders status delivered or cancelled", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "350", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Return orders where **status** is delivered or cancelled.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b77a3fe74e0db37369"}, {"id": "mongo-12-prob-3", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b37a3fe74e0db37195", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b37a3fe74e0db37195", "name": "Problem #496: Find users age over 50 or city Delhi", "title": "Problem #496: Find users age over 50 or city Delhi", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "496", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Return users where **age** > 50 or **city** is \\"Delhi\\". Use **$or**.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b37a3fe74e0db37195"}, {"id": "mongo-12-prob-4", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b37a3fe74e0db37192", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b37a3fe74e0db37192", "name": "Problem #497: Find users with age greater than 40 and city Mumbai", "title": "Problem #497: Find users with age greater than 40 and city Mumbai", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "497", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Return users where **age** > 40 and **city** is \\"Mumbai\\". Use **$and** (or multiple keys).", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b37a3fe74e0db37192"}, {"id": "mongo-12-prob-5", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9c27a3fe74e0db37787", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9c27a3fe74e0db37787", "name": "Problem #4: Reviews with 