pression on a specific field: `{ <field>: { $not: { <$operator>: <value> } } }`. Unlike `$and`, `$or`, and `$nor`, `$not` takes a single condition object (NOT an array) and is placed inside the field key.\n\n### 🛠️ Practical Logical Operator Queries\n```javascript\n// 1. $and: Students with age strictly between 20 and 25 (21, 22, 23, 24)\ndb.students.find({\n  $and: [\n    { age: { $gt: 20 } },\n    { age: { $lt: 25 } }\n  \n}, { name: 1, age: 1, class: 1, _id: 0 })\n\n// 2. $and across different fields: Age > 20 AND Class is "BTech"\ndb.students.find({\n  $and: [\n    { age: { $gt: 20 } },\n    { class: { $eq: "BTech" } }\n  \n})\n\n// 3. $or: Students who are EITHER older than 20 OR enrolled in "BTech"\ndb.students.find({\n  $or: [\n    { age: { $gt: 20 } },\n    { class: { $eq: "BTech" } }\n  \n})\n\n// 4. $nor: Students who are NEITHER older than 20 NOR enrolled in "BTech"\ndb.students.find({\n  $nor: [\n    { age: { $gt: 20 } },\n    { class: { $eq: "BTech" } }\n  \n})\n\n// 5. $not (Field-Level): Students whose age is NOT greater than 20 (i.e. <= 20)\ndb.students.find({\n  age: { $not: { $gt: 20 } }\n})\n\n// 6. Using $and inside deleteMany()\ndb.students.deleteMany({\n  $and: [\n    { age: { $gt: 20 } },\n    { class: { $eq: "BTech" } }\n  \n})\n```\n\n### ⚠️ Common Syntax Mistakes\n* **Placing `$not` at the Top Level or Passing an Array:** `$not` must always be nested inside a field (`{ age: { $not: { $gt: 20 } } }`). Writing `{ $not: [ ...  }` at the top level throws an `unknown top level operator: $not` error.	Yahoo Baba	https://www.youtube.com/@YahooBaba	655	Lecture 12: Logical Query Operators — $and, $or, $nor & $not	Combine multiple filter conditions across single or multiple fields in find(), updateMany(), and deleteMany() using MongoDB logical operators: $and, $or, $nor, and $not.	20	Easy	\N	12	[{"id": "mongo-12-prob-1", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bf7a3fe74e0db3765d", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mon