ice-questions/69aab9c17a3fe74e0db37706", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9c17a3fe74e0db37706", "name": "Problem #47: Find reviews by userId 14", "title": "Problem #47: Find reviews by userId 14", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "47", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Return reviews where userId is 14.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9c17a3fe74e0db37706"}, {"id": "mongo-12-prob-9", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9c17a3fe74e0db37703", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9c17a3fe74e0db37703", "name": "Problem #48: Find reviews by productId 14", "title": "Problem #48: Find reviews by productId 14", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "48", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Return reviews where productId is 14.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9c17a3fe74e0db37703"}, {"id": "mongo-12-prob-10", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9c07a3fe74e0db3768a", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9c07a3fe74e0db3768a", "name": "Problem #87: Find inventory with sku matching SKU-1", "title": "Problem #87: Find inventory with sku matching SKU-1", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "87", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Return inventory where **sku** starts with \\"SKU-1\\". Use **$regex**.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9c07a3fe74e0db3768a"}]	https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/query-logical/	\N	\N	\N
22098	Lecture 13: Element Query Operators — $exists & $type (BSON Type Filtering)	mongo-lecture-13-element-query-operators-exists-type	Filter documents by field presence or absence using $exists and audit or query fields by their underlying BSON storage type using $type.	2026-10-06 19:28:34.895846+05:30	### 📌 Topic Overview\nBecause MongoDB has a flexible schema, some documents in a collection may omit optional fields or accidentally store values in the wrong data type (such as storing `age: "24"` as a String instead of an Integer). **Element Query Operators** (`$exists` and `$type`) let you query metadata about fields rather than their values.\n\n### 💡 Core Element Operators\n* **`$exists` (Field Presence Check):** Syntax: `{ <field>: { $exists: <true | false> } }`\n  * **`true`:** Matches all documents that contain the specified field (including documents where the field value is `null`).\n  * **`false`:** Matches all documents where the specified field is completely missing.\n* **`$type` (BSON Data Type Check):** Syntax: `{ <field>: { $type: <BSON alias | number | array> } }`\n  * Matches documents where the value of `<field>` is stored as the specified BSON type.\n  * Common BSON string aliases: `"string"` (code `2`), `"int"` (32-bit integer, code `16`), `"long"` (64-bit integer, code `18`), `"double"` (code `1`), `"bool"` (code `8`), `"date"` (code `9`), `"array"` (code `4`), `"object"` (code `3`), `"null"` (code `10`).\n  * **Multiple Types:** Pass an array of types (e.g., `{ age: { $type: ["double", "int" } }`) to match documents where the field is either a 32-bit integer or a floating-point double.\n\n### 🛠️ Practical $exists & $type Queries\n```javascript\n// 1. Find students where the "class" field is completely missing\ndb.students.find({\n  class: { $exists: false }\n})\n\n// 2. Find students where the "class" field exists\ndb.students.find({\n  class: { $exists: true }\n})\n\n// 3. Data Auditing: Find records where "age" was mistakenly stored as a String ("24")\ndb.students.find({\n  age: { $type: "string" }\n})\n\n// 4. Find records where "age" is strictly a 32-bit Integer ("int")\ndb.students.find({\n  age: { $type: "int" }\n})\n\n// 5. Find records where "age" is EITHER a Double OR a 32-bit Integer\ndb.students.find({\n  age: { $type: ["double", "int" }\n})\n\n// 6. Querying by numeric BSON type code (1 = "double")\ndb.students.find({\n  age: { $type: 1 }\n})\n```	[{"url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/query-element/", "link": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/query-element/", "title": "MongoDB Official Manual — Lecture 13: Element Query Operators"}]	[{"url": "http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NnWG59wMYIs", "title": "MongoDB Element Query Operators Tutorial in Hindi / Urdu", "duration": "11m", "creator_name": "Yahoo Baba", "creator_channel_url": "https://www.youtube.com/@YahooBaba"}]	[{"id": "mongo-13-prob-1", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bf7a3fe74e0db37675", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bf7a3fe74e0db37675", "name": "Problem #94: Find inventory with location type Point", "title": "Problem #94: Find inventory with location type Point", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "94", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Return inventory where **location.type** is \\"Point\\". Use dot notation.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bf7a3fe74e0db37675"}, {"id": "mongo-13-prob-2", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bf7a3fe74e0db3765a", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bf7a3fe74e0db3765a", "name": "Problem #103: Find reviews with text exists", "title": "Problem #103: Find reviews with text exists", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "103", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Return reviews that have a **text** field. Use **$exists**.", "external_url": "https://mon