22099	Lecture 14: Evaluation Query Operators — $regex, $expr, $mod & $jsonSchema	mongo-lecture-14-evaluation-query-operators-regex-expr-mod	Perform pattern matching with $regex, compare fields within the same document using $expr and arithmetic operators, and filter by division remainders with $mod.	2026-10-06 19:28:34.895846+05:30	### 📌 Topic Overview\n**Evaluation Query Operators** unlock advanced search capabilities that standard comparison operators cannot express: pattern matching inside strings (`$regex`), comparing two fields inside the same document (`$expr`), and modulo arithmetic filtering (`$mod`).\n\n### 💡 Core Evaluation Operators\n* **`$regex` (Regular Expression Pattern Matching):**\n  * **Substring Match:** `{ name: { $regex: "Khan" } }` matches `"Khan"` anywhere in the string (case-sensitive by default).\n  * **Case-Insensitive Match (`i` flag):** Use slash notation `{ name: { $regex: /khan/i } }` or `{ name: { $regex: "khan", $options: "i" } }` to ignore letter casing.\n  * **Starts With (`^`):** `{ name: { $regex: "^A" } }` matches names starting with `A` (e.g., `"Akshay Kumar"`, `"Aamir Khan"`).\n  * **Ends With (`$`):** `{ name: { $regex: "or$" } }` matches names ending with `"or"` (e.g., `"Shahid Kapoor"`).\n* **`$expr` (Intra-Document Field Comparison & Aggregation Expressions):**\n  * Allows using aggregation expressions (like `$gt`, `$lt`, `$multiply`, `$add`) inside `find()` to compare two fields in the **same document**.\n  * Field references inside `$expr` must be prefixed with a dollar sign (`"$spent"`, `"$budget"`).\n* **`$mod` (Modulo Division Filter):**\n  * Syntax: `{ <field>: { $mod: [ <divisor>, <remainder>  } }`.\n  * Divides the numeric field value by `<divisor>` and matches documents where the remainder equals `<remainder>` (e.g., `[2, 0` for even numbers, `[7, 0` for multiples of 7).\n\n### 🛠️ Practical Evaluation Operator Examples\n```javascript\n// 1. $regex: Case-insensitive substring, prefix (^), and suffix ($) searches\ndb.students.find({ name: { $regex: /khan/i } })\ndb.students.find({ name: { $regex: "^A" } })\ndb.students.find({ name: { $regex: "or$" } })\n\n// 2. $expr: Find monthlyBudget categories where "spent" exceeded "budget"\ndb.monthlyBudget.find({\n  $expr: {\n    $gt: ["$spent", "$budget"\n  }\n})\n\n// 3. $expr with $multiply: Find products where selling "price" > 1.2x "cost"\ndb.sales.find({\n  $expr: {\n    $gt: [\n      "$price",\n      { $multiply: ["$cost", 1.2 }\n    \n  }\n})\n\n// 4. $mod: Find sales items whose "cost" is cleanly divisible by 7 (remainder 0)\ndb.sales.find({\n  cost: { $mod: [7, 0 }\n})\n```	[{"url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/query-evaluation/", "link": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/query-evaluation/", "title": "MongoDB Official Manual — Lecture 14: Evaluation Query Operators"}]	[{"url": "http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bYgbqchjtgI", "title": "MongoDB Evaluation Query Operators Tutorial in Hindi / Urdu", "duration": "23m", "creator_name": "Yahoo Baba", "creator_channel_url": "https://www.youtube.com/@YahooBaba"}]	[{"id": "mongo-14-prob-1", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bf7a3fe74e0db37621", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bf7a3fe74e0db37621", "name": "Problem #122: Find log message containing 15", "title": "Problem #122: Find log message containing 15", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "122", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Return logs where message contains \\"15\\". Use $regex.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bf7a3fe74e0db37621"}, {"id": "mongo-14-prob-2", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bd7a3fe74e0db3758b", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bd7a3fe74e0db3758b", "name": "Problem #172: Find logs with message containing Log", "title": "Problem #172: Find logs with message containing Log", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "172", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Return logs where **message** contains \\"Log\\". Use **$regex**.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bd7a3fe74e0db3758b"}, {"id": "mongo-14-prob-3", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bd7a3fe74e0db37588", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bd7a3fe74e0db37588", "name": "Problem #173: Find articles with title containing Article", "title": "Problem #173: Find articles with title containing Article", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "173", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Return articles where **title** contains \\"Article\\". Use **$regex**.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bd7a3fe74e0db37588"}, {"id": "mongo-14-prob-4", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b77a3fe74e0db3733f", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b77a3fe74e0db3733f", "name": "Problem #364: Customers with email containing mail", "title": "Problem #364: Customers with email containing mail", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "364", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Return customers where **email** contains \\"mail\\". Use **$regex**.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b77a3fe74e0db3733f"}, {"id": "mongo-14-prob-5", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b77a3fe74e0db3733c", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b77a3fe74e0db3733c", "name": "Problem #365: Find products with name containing Product 1", "title": "Problem #365: Find products with name containing Product 1", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "365", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Return products where **name** starts with \\"Product 1\\". Use **$regex**.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b77a3fe74e0db3733c"}, {"id": "mongo-14-prob-6", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b67a3fe74e0db3728e", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b67a3fe74e0db3728e", "name": "Problem #423: Find departments with name containing Sales", "title": "Problem #423: Find departments with name containing Sales", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "423", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Return departments where **name** contains \\"Sales\\". Use **$regex**.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b67a3fe74e0db3728e"}, {"id": "mongo-14-prob-7", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b57a3fe74e0db37273", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b57a3fe74e0db37273", "name": "Problem #432: Users with email containing example", "title": "Problem #432: Users with email containing example", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "432", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Return users where **email** contains the string \\"example\\". Use **$regex**.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b57a3fe74e0db37273"}, {"id": "mongo-14-prob-8", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b47a3fe74e0db371e0", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b47a3fe74e0db371e0", "name": "Problem #471: Find users with name matching User followed by digits", "title": "Problem #471: Find users with name matching User followed by digits", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "471", "difficulty": "Hard", "description": "Return users where **name** matches pattern User followed by one or more digits. Use **$regex**.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b47a3fe74e0db371e0"}, {"id": "mongo-14-prob-9", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b37a3fe74e0db3718f", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b37a3fe74e0db3718f", "name": "Problem #498: Find users with email ending with example.com", "title": "Problem #498: Find users with email ending with example.com", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "498", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Return users where **email** ends with \\"example.com\\". Use **$regex**.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b37a3fe74e0db3718f"}, {"id": "mongo-14-prob-10", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b37a3fe74e0db3718c", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b37a3fe74e0db3718c", "name": "Problem #499: Find users with name containing User1", "title": "Problem #499: Find users with name containing User1", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "499", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Return users where **name** starts with \\"User1\\". Use **$regex**.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b37a3fe74e0db3718c"}]	\N	### 📌 Topic Overview\n**Evaluation Query Operators** unlock advanced search capabilities that standard comparison operators cannot express: pattern matching inside strings (`$regex`), comparing two fields inside the same document (`$expr`), and modulo arithmetic filtering (`$mod`).\n\n### 💡 Core Evaluation Operators\n* **`$regex` (Regular Expression Pattern Matching):**\n  * **Substring Match:** `{ name: { $regex: "Khan" } }` matches `"Khan"` anywhere in the string (case-sensitive by default).\n  * **Case-Insensitive Match (`i` flag):** Use slash notation `{ name: { $regex: /khan/i } }` or `{ name: { $regex: "khan", $options: "i" } }` to ignore letter casing.\n  * **Starts With (`^`):** `{ name: { $regex: "^A" } }` matches names starting with `A` (e.g., `"Akshay Kumar"`, `"Aamir Khan"`).\n  * **Ends With (`$`):** `{ name: { $regex: "or$" } }` matches names ending with `"or"` (e.g., `"Shahid Kapoor"`).\n* **`$expr` (Intra-Document Field Comparison & Aggregation Expressions):**\n  * Allows using aggregation expressions (like `$gt`, `$lt`, `$multiply`, `$add`) inside `find()` to compare two fields in the **same document**.\n  * Field references inside `$expr` must be prefixed with a dollar sign (`"$spent"`, `"$budget"`).\n* **`$mod` (Modulo Division Filter):**\n  * Syntax: `{ <field>: { $mod: [ <divisor>, <remainder>  } }`.\n  * Divides the numeric field value by `<divisor>` and matches documents where the remainder equals `<remainder>` (e.g., `[2, 0` for even numbers, `[7, 0` for multiples of 7).\n\n### 🛠️ Practical Evaluation Operator Examples\n```javascript\n// 1. $regex: Case-insensitive substring, prefix (^), and suffix ($) searches\ndb.students.find({ name: { $regex: /khan/i } })\ndb.students.find({ name: { $regex: "^A" } })\ndb.students.find({ name: { $regex: "or$" } })\n\n// 2. $expr: Find monthlyBudget categories where "spent" exceeded "budget"\ndb.monthlyBudget.find({\n  $expr: {\n    $gt: ["$spent", "$budget"\n  }\n})\n\n// 3. $expr with $multiply: Find products where selling "price" > 1.2x "cost"\ndb.sales.find({\n  $expr: {\n    $gt: [\n      "$price",\n      { $multiply: ["$cost", 1.2 }\n    \n  }\n})\n\n// 4. $mod: Find sales items whose "cost" is cleanly divisible by 7 (remainder 0)\ndb.sales.find({\n  cost: { $mod: [7, 0 }\n})\n```	Yahoo Baba	https://www.youtube.com/@YahooBaba	655	Lecture 14: Evaluation Query Operators — $regex, $expr, $mod & $jsonSchema	Perform pattern matching with $regex, compare fields within the same document using $expr and arithmetic operators, and filter by division remainders with $mod.	20	Easy	\N	14	[{"id": "mongo-14-prob-1", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bf7a3fe74e0db37621", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bf7a3fe74e0db37621", "name": "Problem #122: Find log message containing 15", "title": "Problem #122: Find log message containing 15", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "122", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Return logs where message contains \\"15\\". Use $regex.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bf7a3fe74e0db37621"}, {"id": "mongo-14-prob-2", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bd7a3fe74e0db3758b", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bd7a3fe74e0db3758b", "name": "Problem #172: Find logs with message containing Log", "title": "Problem #172: Find logs with message containing Log", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "172", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Return logs where **message** contains \\"Log\\". Use **$regex**.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bd7a3fe74e0db3758b"}, {"id": "mongo-14-prob-3", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bd7a3fe74e0db37588", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bd7a3fe74e0db37588", "name": "Problem #173: Find articles with title containing Article", "title": "Problem #173: Find articles with title containing Article", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "173", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Return articles where **title** contains \\"Article\\". Use **$regex**.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bd7a3fe74e0db37588"}, {"id": "mongo-14-prob-4", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b77a3fe74e0db3733f", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b77a3fe74e0db3733f", "name": "Problem #364: Customers with email containing mail", "title": "Problem #364: Customers with email containing mail", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "364", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Return customers where **email** contains \\"mail\\". Use **$regex**.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b77a3fe74e0db3733f"}, {"id": "mongo-14-prob-5", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b77a3fe74e0db3733c", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b77a3fe74e0db3733c", "name": "Problem #365: Find products with name containing Product 1", "title": "Problem #365: Find products with name containing Product 1", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "365", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Return products where **name** starts with \\"Product 1\\". Use **$regex**.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b77a3fe74e0db3733c"}, {"id": "mongo-14-prob-6", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b67a3fe74e0db3728e", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b67a3fe74e0db3728e", "name": "Problem #423: Find departments with name containing Sales", "title": "Problem #423: Find departments with name containing Sales", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "423", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Return departments where **name** contains \\"Sales\\". Use **$regex**.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b67a3fe74e0db3728e"}, {"id": "mongo-14-prob-7", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b57a3fe74e0db37273", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b57a3fe74e0db37273", "name": "Problem #432: Users with email containing example", "title": "Problem #432: Users with email containing example", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "432", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Return users where **email** contains the string \\"example\\". Use **$regex**.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b57a3fe74e0db37273"}, {"id": "mongo-14-prob-8", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b47a3fe74e0db371e0", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b47a3fe74e0db371e0", "name": "Problem #471: Find users with name matching User followed by digits", "title": "Problem #471: Find users with name matching User followed by digits", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "471", "difficulty": "Hard", "description": "Return users where **name** matches pattern User followed by one or more digits. Use **$regex**.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b47a3fe74e0db371e0"}, {"id": "mongo-14-prob-9", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b37a3fe74e0db3718f", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b37a3fe74e0db3718f", "name": "Problem #498: Find users with email ending with example.com", "title": "Problem #498: Find users with email ending with example.com", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "498", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Return users where **email** ends with \\"example.com\\". Use **$regex**.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b37a3fe74e0db3718f"}, {"id": "mongo-14-prob-10", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b37a3fe74e0db3718c", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b37a3fe74e0db3718c", "name": "Problem #499: Find users with name containing User1", "title": "Problem #499: Find users with name containing User1", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "499", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Return users where **name** starts with \\"User1\\". Use **$regex**.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b37a3fe74e0db3718c"}]	https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/query-evaluation/	\N	\N	\N
22100	Lecture 15: Atomic Find-and-Modify — findOneAndUpdate(), findOneAndReplace() & findOneAndDelete()	mongo-lecture-15-findoneandupdate-findoneandreplace-findoneanddelete	Atomically locate, modify, and return documents in a single round-trip using findOneAndUpdate(), findOneAndReplace(), and findOneAndDelete() with returnDocument, upsert, sort, and projection options.	2026-10-06 19:28:34.895846+05:30	### 📌 Topic Overview\nWhile `updateOne()`, `replaceOne()`, and `deleteOne()` only return status metadata (`{ acknowledged: true, modifiedCount: 1 }`), real-world backend APIs usually need the **actual document** back after modifying or deleting it. MongoDB provides three atomic methods that find, modify, and return the target document in a single operation:\n* **`findOneAndUpdate(filter, update, options)`**\n* **`findOneAndReplace(filter, replacement, options)`**\n* **`findOneAndDelete(filter, options)`**\n\n### 💡 Key Options Parameters\n* **`returnDocument: "before" | "after"`:**\n  * `"before"` (Default): Returns the original document state **before** the update/replacement was applied.\n  * `"after"`: Returns the newly modified document state **after** the update/replacement was applied.\n* **`projection: { field: 1, _id: 0 }`:** Shapes which fields are included in the returned document.\n* **`upsert: true | false`:** Available on `findOneAndUpdate` and `findOneAndReplace`. When `true`, if no document matches `filter`, MongoDB inserts a new document instead of returning `null`.\n* **`sort: { field: 1 | -1 }`:** When multiple documents match `filter` (e.g., two students named `"Salman Khan"`), `sort` determines which specific document gets updated, replaced, or deleted first (e.g., `{ age: 1 }` targets the youngest matching student).\n\n### 🛠️ Practical Atomic Find-and-Modify Examples\n```javascript\n// 1. findOneAndUpdate: Update age, return the UPDATED document ("after"), and project fields\ndb.students.findOneAndUpdate(\n  { name: "Kartik Aaryan" },\n  { $set: { age: 25 } },\n  {\n    returnDocument: "after",\n    projection: { name: 1, age: 1, _id: 0 }\n  }\n)\n\n// 2. findOneAndUpdate with upsert: Insert if student does not exist\ndb.students.findOneAndUpdate(\n  { name: "Sachin Tendulkar" },\n  { $set: { age: 25, class: "BIT" } },\n  {\n    returnDocument: "after",\n    upsert: true\n  }\n)\n\n// 3. findOneAndUpdate with sort: Among duplicate names, update the youngest student (age: 1)\ndb.students.findOneAndUpdate(\n  { name: "Salman Khan" },\n  { $set: { class: "BIT" } },\n  { sort: { age: 1 }, returnDocument: "after" }\n)\n\n// 4. findOneAndReplace: Replace entire document while preserving _id\ndb.students.findOneAndReplace(\n  { name: "Akshay Kumar" },\n  { name: "Sanjay Dutt", age: 35, class: "BCom" },\n  { returnDocument: "after" }\n)\n\n// 5. findOneAndDelete: Delete youngest matching record and return its deleted data\ndb.students.findOneAndDelete(\n  { name: "Salman Khan" },\n  {\n    sort: { age: 1 },\n    projection: { name: 1, _id: 0 }\n  }\n)\n```	[{"url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/method/db.collection.findOneAndUpdate/", "link": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/method/db.collection.findOneAndUpdate/", "title": "MongoDB Official Manual — Lecture 15: Atomic Find-and-Modify"}]	[{"url": "http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8EuluG46ysk", "title": "MongoDB FindOneAndUpdate FindOneAndReplace FindOneAndDelete Tutorial in Hindi / Urdu", "duration": "26m", "creator_name": "Yahoo Baba", "creator_channel_url": "https://www.youtube.com/@YahooBaba"}]	[{"id": "mongo-15-prob-1", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bd7a3fe74e0db37591", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bd7a3fe74e0db37591", "name": "Problem #170: Articles with tags size 3", "title": "Problem #170: Articles with tags size 3", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "170", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Return articles that have exactly 3 tags.", "ex