, "name": "Problem #228: Articles with tag node", "title": "Problem #228: Articles with tag node", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "228", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Return articles that have \\"node\\" in **tags**.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bb7a3fe74e0db374e1"}, {"id": "mongo-15-prob-6", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bb7a3fe74e0db374de", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bb7a3fe74e0db374de", "name": "Problem #229: Articles with tag js", "title": "Problem #229: Articles with tag js", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "229", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Return articles that have \\"js\\" in **tags**.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bb7a3fe74e0db374de"}, {"id": "mongo-15-prob-7", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bb7a3fe74e0db374db", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bb7a3fe74e0db374db", "name": "Problem #230: Articles with tag mongodb", "title": "Problem #230: Articles with tag mongodb", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "230", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Return articles that have \\"mongodb\\" in **tags**.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bb7a3fe74e0db374db"}, {"id": "mongo-15-prob-8", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9ba7a3fe74e0db3742d", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9ba7a3fe74e0db3742d", "name": "Problem #286: Products attributes color green", "title": "Problem #286: Products attributes color green", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "286", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Return products where attributes.color is \\"green\\".", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9ba7a3fe74e0db3742d"}, {"id": "mongo-15-prob-9", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9ba7a3fe74e0db3742a", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9ba7a3fe74e0db3742a", "name": "Problem #287: Products attributes color blue", "title": "Problem #287: Products attributes color blue", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "287", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Return products where attributes.color is \\"blue\\".", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9ba7a3fe74e0db3742a"}, {"id": "mongo-15-prob-10", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9ba7a3fe74e0db37427", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9ba7a3fe74e0db37427", "name": "Problem #288: Products attributes size L", "title": "Problem #288: Products attributes size L", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "288", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Return products where attributes.size is \\"L\\".", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9ba7a3fe74e0db37427"}]	\N	### 📌 Topic Overview\nWhile `updateOne()`, `replaceOne()`, and `deleteOne()` only return status metadata (`{ acknowledged: true, modifiedCount: 1 }`), real-world backend APIs usually need the **actual document** back after modifying or deleting it. MongoDB provides three atomic methods that find, modify, and return the target document in a single operation:\n* **`findOneAndUpdate(filter, update, options)`**\n* **`findOneAndReplace(filter, replacement, options)`**\n* **`findOneAndDelete(filter, options)`**\n\n### 💡 Key Options Parameters\n* **`returnDocument: "before" | "after"`:**\n  * `"before"` (Default): Returns the original document state **before** the update/replacement was applied.\n  * `"after"`: Returns the newly modified document state **after** the update/replacement was applied.\n* **`projection: { field: 1, _id: 0 }`:** Shapes which fields are included in the returned document.\n* **`upsert: true | false`:** Available on `findOneAndUpdate` and `findOneAndReplace`. When `true`, if no document matches `filter`, MongoDB inserts a new document instead of returning `null`.\n* **`sort: { field: 1 | -1 }`:** When multiple documents match `filter` (e.g., two students named `"Salman Khan"`), `sort` determines which specific document gets updated, replaced, or deleted first (e.g., `{ age: 1 }` targets the youngest matching student).\n\n### 🛠️ Practical Atomic Find-and-Modify Examples\n```javascript\n// 1. findOneAndUpdate: Update age, return the UPDATED document ("after"), and project fields\ndb.students.findOneAndUpdate(\n  { name: "Kartik Aaryan" },\n  { $set: { age: 25 } },\n  {\n    returnDocument: "after",\n    projection: { name: 1, age: 1, _id: 0 }\n  }\n)\n\n// 2. findOneAndUpdate with upsert: Insert if student does not exist\ndb.students.findOneAndUpdate(\n  { name: "Sachin Tendulkar" },\n  { $set: { age: 25, class: "BIT" } },\n  {\n    returnDocument: "after",\n    upsert: true\n  }\n)\n\n// 3. findOneAndUpdate with sort: Among duplicate names, update the youngest student (age: 1)\ndb.students.findOneAndUpdate(\n  { name: "Salman Khan" },\n  { $set: { class: "BIT" } },\n  { sort: { age: 1 }, returnDocument: "after" }\n)\n\n// 4. findOneAndReplace: Replace entire document while preserving _id\ndb.students.findOneAndReplace(\n  { name: "Akshay Kumar" },\n  { name: "Sanjay Dutt", age: 35, class: "BCom" },\n  { returnDocument: "after" }\n)\n\n// 5. findOneAndDelete: Delete youngest matching record and return its deleted data\ndb.students.findOneAndDelete(\n  { name: "Salman Khan" },\n  {\n    sort: { age: 1 },\n    projection: { name: 1, _id: 0 }\n  }\n)\n```	Yahoo Baba	https://www.youtube.com/@YahooBaba	655	Lecture 15: Atomic Find-and-Modify — findOneAndUpdate(), findOneAndReplace() & findOneAndDelete()	Atomically locate, modify, and return documents in a single round-trip using findOneAndUpdate(), findOneAndReplace(), and findOneAndDelete() with returnDocument, upsert, sort, and projection options.	20	Easy	\N	15	[{"id": "mongo-15-prob-1", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bd7a3fe74e0db37591", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bd7a3fe74e0db37591", "name": "Problem #170: Articles with tags size 3", "title": "Problem #170: Articles with tags size 3", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "170", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Return articles that have exactly 3 tags.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bd7a3fe74e0db37591"}, {"id": "mongo-15-prob-2", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bd7a3fe74e0db37582", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bd7a3fe74e0db37582", "name": "Problem #175: Find logs with meta.userId 20", "title": "Problem #175: Find logs with meta.userId 20", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "175", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Return logs where meta.userId is 20.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bd7a3fe74e0db37582"}, {"id": "mongo-15-prob-3", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bc7a3fe74e0db374fc", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bc7a3fe74e0db374fc", "name": "Problem #219: Find articles with views between 500 and 2000", "title": "Problem #219: Find articles with views between 500 and 2000", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "219", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Return articles where **views** is between 500 and 2000.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bc7a3fe74e0db374fc"}, {"id": "mongo-15-prob-4", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bb7a3fe74e0db374e4", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab