b"}, {"id": "mongo-15-prob-8", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9ba7a3fe74e0db3742d", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9ba7a3fe74e0db3742d", "name": "Problem #286: Products attributes color green", "title": "Problem #286: Products attributes color green", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "286", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Return products where attributes.color is \\"green\\".", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9ba7a3fe74e0db3742d"}, {"id": "mongo-15-prob-9", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9ba7a3fe74e0db3742a", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9ba7a3fe74e0db3742a", "name": "Problem #287: Products attributes color blue", "title": "Problem #287: Products attributes color blue", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "287", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Return products where attributes.color is \\"blue\\".", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9ba7a3fe74e0db3742a"}, {"id": "mongo-15-prob-10", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9ba7a3fe74e0db37427", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9ba7a3fe74e0db37427", "name": "Problem #288: Products attributes size L", "title": "Problem #288: Products attributes size L", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "288", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Return products where attributes.size is \\"L\\".", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9ba7a3fe74e0db37427"}]	https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/method/db.collection.findOneAndUpdate/	\N	\N	\N
22078	Lecture 20: Grouping Data — GROUP BY, HAVING vs. WHERE & SQL Execution Order	pg-lecture-20-group-by-and-having-clauses	Bucket rows into summary groups with GROUP BY, filter aggregated buckets using HAVING, and master the internal SQL query execution pipeline.	2026-10-05 19:34:44.247876+05:30	### 🎯 Engineering Guide: Lecture 20: Grouping Data — GROUP BY, HAVING vs. WHERE & SQL Execution Order\nPart of the **PostgreSQL & Relational SQL Mastery** curriculum designed for modern software development.\n\n- **Core Concepts**: Architectural patterns, modular design principles, and production best practices.\n- **Hands-on Objective**: Understand the lifecycle, error boundaries, and integration points with the rest of the application stack.\n- **Production Checklist**:\n  - Clean separation of concerns (controller, service, repository layers).\n  - Robust error handling and structured logging.\n  - Unit and integration testing considerations.	[{"url": "https://developer.mozilla.org/", "title": "MDN Web Docs"}, {"url": "https://devdocs.io/", "title": "Official Documentation & API Reference"}]	[{"url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FsTXg74UJzE", "title": "PostgreSQL GROUP BY & HAVING Clause Explained with Practical Questions", "duration": "18m", "creator_name": "Thapa Technical (Vinod Bahadur Thapa)", "creator_channel_url": "https://www.youtube.com/@ThapaTechnical"}]	[{"id": "pg-20-prob-1", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/classes-more-than-5-students/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/classes-more-than-5-students/", "name": "Classes More Than 5 Students (GROUP BY + HAVING COUNT)", "title": "Classes More Than 5 Students (GROUP BY + HAVING COUNT)", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "20_1", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Solve \\"Classes More Than 5 Students (GROUP BY + HAVING COUNT)\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/classes-more-than-5-students/"}, {"id": "pg-20-prob-2", "url": "https://leetcode.com/p