e", "problemId": "414", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Execute: Find users with tag5.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b67a3fe74e0db372a9"}, {"id": "mongo-20-prob-5", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b67a3fe74e0db372a6", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b67a3fe74e0db372a6", "name": "Problem #415: Find users with tag4", "title": "Problem #415: Find users with tag4", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "415", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Execute: Find users with tag4.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b67a3fe74e0db372a6"}, {"id": "mongo-20-prob-6", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b67a3fe74e0db372a3", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b67a3fe74e0db372a3", "name": "Problem #416: Find users with tag3", "title": "Problem #416: Find users with tag3", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "416", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Execute: Find users with tag3.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b67a3fe74e0db372a3"}, {"id": "mongo-20-prob-7", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b47a3fe74e0db371f5", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b47a3fe74e0db371f5", "name": "Problem #464: Add field fullLabel in aggregation", "title": "Problem #464: Add field fullLabel in aggregation", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "464", "difficulty": "Hard", "description": "Aggregation: from **departments**, add a field **fullLabel** as name + \\" - \\" + location. Use **$addFields** and **$concat**.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b47a3fe74e0db371f5"}, {"id": "mongo-20-prob-8", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b37a3fe74e0db371a7", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b37a3fe74e0db371a7", "name": "Problem #490: Find users where tags array contains tag1", "title": "Problem #490: Find users where tags array contains tag1", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "490", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Return users whose **tags** array contains the string \\"tag1\\".", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b37a3fe74e0db371a7"}, {"id": "mongo-20-prob-9", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bd7a3fe74e0db3758e", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bd7a3fe74e0db3758e", "name": "Problem #171: Articles with tags size 2", "title": "Problem #171: Articles with tags size 2", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "171", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Return articles that have exactly 2 tags. Use **$size**.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bd7a3fe74e0db3758e"}, {"id": "mongo-20-prob-10", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bf7a3fe74e0db37651", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bf7a3fe74e0db37651", "name": "Problem #106: Find inventory with sku SKU-1001", "title": "Problem #106: Find inventory with sku SKU-1001", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "106", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Return the inventory document with **sku** \\"SKU-1001\\".", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bf7a3fe74e0db37651"}]	https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/addFields/	\N	\N	\N
22106	Lecture 21: Cross-Collection Pipeline Stages — $out, $merge & $unionWith	mongo-lecture-21-aggregation-out-merge-unionwith	Materialize aggregation results into new collections using $out, incrementally merge or upsert pipeline outputs into existing collections with $merge, and combine multi-collection datasets on read with $unionWith.	2026-10-06 19:28:34.895846+05:30	### 📌 Topic Overview\nMongoDB provides three aggregation stages for working across multiple collections: **`$out`** (writes pipeline output into a brand-new or replaced collection), **`$merge`** (merges pipeline output into an existing collection without wiping non-matching data), and **`$unionWith`** (combines documents from two collections into a single read result set).\n\n### 💡 Comparing `$out`, `$merge`, and `$unionWith`\n* **`$out: "<targetCollection>"` (Terminal Stage):**\n  * Creates a new collection containing the pipeline's output documents.\n  * **Warning:** If `<targetCollection>` already exists, `$out` **completely replaces** its existing contents with the new pipeline output.\n* **`$merge: { into, on, whenMatched, whenNotMatched }` (Terminal Stage):**\n  * Writes pipeline results into an existing collection while preserving existing fields or non-matching documents:\n  * **`into`:** Target collection name (e.g., `"students"`).\n  * **`on`:** Unique matching key shared by both collections (e.g., `"_id"`).\n  * **`whenMatched`:** Action when `on` matches: `"merge"` (combines new fields into existing document), `"replace"` (overwrites existing document), `"keepExisting"`, or `"fail"`.\n  * **`whenNotMatched`:** Action when `on` does not match: `"insert"` (upserts as new document), `"discard"`, or `"fail"`.\n* **`$unionWith: { coll: "<otherCollection>" }` (Read-Only Stage):**\n  * Appends all documents from `<otherCollection>` directly into the current aggregation stream (similar to `UNION ALL` in SQL) without modifying any stored collection on disk.\n\n### 🛠️ Practical $out, $merge & $unionWith Pipelines\n```javascript\n// 1. $out: Group students by class and save the summary into a new "class_data" collection\ndb.students.aggregate([\n  {\n    $group: {\n      _id: "$class",\n      students: { $push: "$name" }\n    }\n  },\n  { $out: "class_data" }\n)\n\n// 2. $merge: Merge "city" and "phone" from "personal" collection into "students" on "_id"\ndb.personal.aggregate([\n  {\n    $merge: {\n      into: "students",\n      on: "_id",\n      whenMatched: "merge",\n      whenNotMatched: "insert"\n    }\n  }\n)\n\n// 3. $unionWith: Combine current students ("students1") and alumni ("students2") in a single query\ndb.students1.aggregate([\n  {\n    $unionWith: {\n      coll: "students2"\n    }\n  }\n)\n```	[{"url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/merge/", "link": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/merge/", "title": "MongoDB Official Manual — Lecture 21: Cross-Collection Pipeline Stages"}]	[{"url": "http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jVw89Bh8zPE", "title": "MongoDB $out $merge & $unionWith Operator Tutorial in Hindi / Urdu", "duration": "23m", "creator_name": "Yahoo Baba", "creator_channel_url": "https://www.youtube.com/@YahooBaba"}]	[{"id": "mongo-21-prob-1", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bf7a3fe74e0db3762d", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bf7a3fe74e0db3762d", "name": "Problem #118: Find all reviews", "title": "Problem #118: Find all reviews", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "118", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Return all documents from **reviews**.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bf7a3fe74e0db3762d"}, {"id": "mongo-21-prob-2", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bf7a3fe74e0db3762a", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bf7a3fe74e0db3762a", "name": "Problem #119: Find all inventory", "title": "Problem #119: Find all inventory", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "119", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Return all documents from **inventory**.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bf7a3fe74e0db3762a"}, {"id": "mongo-21-prob-3", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bb7a3fe74e0db374c6", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bb7a3fe74e0db374c6", "name": "Problem #237: Find all logs", "title": "Problem #237: Find all logs", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "237", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Return all documents from **logs**.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bb7a3fe74e0db374c6"}, {"id": "mongo-21-prob-4", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bb7a3fe74e0db374c3", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bb7a3fe74e0db374c3", "name": "Problem #238: Find all articles", "title": "Problem #238: Find all articles", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "238", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Return all documents from **articles**.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bb7a3fe74e0db374c3"}, {"id": "mongo-21-prob-5", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b67a3fe74e0db372d9", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b67a3fe74e0db372d9", "name": "Problem #398: Find all orders", "title": "Problem #398: Find all orders", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "398", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Return all documents from **orders**.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b67a3fe74e0db372d9"}, {"id": "mongo-21-prob-6", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b67a3fe74e0db372d6", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b67a3fe74e0db372d6", "name": "Problem #399: Find all customers", "title": "Problem #399: Find all customers", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "399", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Return all documents from **customers**.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b67a3fe74e0db372d6"}, {"id": "mongo-21-prob-7", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b67a3fe74e0db372d3", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b67a3fe74e0db372d3", "name": "Problem #400: Find all products", "title": "Problem #400: Find all products", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "400", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Return all documents from **products**.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b67a3fe74e0db372d3"}, {"id": "mongo-21-prob-8", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b67a3fe74e0db372bb", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b67a3fe74e0db372bb", "name": "Problem #408: Sort departments by location", "title": "Problem #408: Sort departments by location", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "408", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Execute: Sort departments by location.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b67a3fe74e0db372bb"}, {"id": "mongo-21-prob-9", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b67a3fe74e0db372a0", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b67a3fe74e0db372a0", "name": "Problem #417: Find departments in Bangalore", "title": "Problem #417: Find departments in Bangalore", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "417", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Execute: Find departments in Bangalore.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b67a3fe74e0db372a0"}, {"id": "mongo-21-prob-10", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b67a3fe74e0db3729a", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b67a3fe74e0db3729a", "name": "Problem #419: Find users with departmentId 5", "title": "Problem #419: Find users with departmentId 5", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "419", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Execute: Find users with departmentId 5.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9b67a3fe74e0db3729a"}]	\N	### 📌 Topic Overview\nMongoDB provides three aggregation stages for working across multiple collections: **`$out`** (writes pipeline output into a brand-new or replaced collection), **`$merge`** (merges pipeline output into an existing collection without wiping non-matching data), and **`$unionWith`** (combines documents from two collections into a single read result set).\n\n### 💡 Comparing `$out`, `$merge`, and `$unionWith`\n* **`$out: "<targetCollection>"` (Terminal Stage):**\n  * Creates a new collection containing the pipeline's output documents.\n  * **Warning:** If `<targetCollection>` already exists, `$out` **completely replaces** its existing contents with the new pipeline output.\n* **`$merge: { into, on, whenMatched, whenNotMatched }` (Terminal Stage):**\n  * Writes pipeline results into an existing collection while preserving existing fields or non-matching documents:\n  * **`into`:** Target collection name (e.g., `"students"`).\n  * **`on`:** Unique matching key shared by both collections (e.g., `"_id"`).\n  * **`whenMatched`:** Action when `on` matches: `"merge"` (combines new fields into existing document), `"replace"` (overwrites existing document), `"keepExisting"`, or `"fail"`.\n  * **`whenNotMatched`:** Action when `on` does not match: `"insert"` (upserts as new document), `"discard"`, or `"fail"`.\n* **`$unionWith: { coll: "<otherCollection>" }` (Read-Only Stage):**\n  * Appends all documents from `<otherCollection>` directly into the current aggregation stream (similar to `UNION ALL` in SQL) without modifying any stored collection on disk.\n\n### 🛠️ Practical $out, $merge & $unionWith Pipelines\n```javascript\n// 1. $out: Group students by class and save the summary into a new "class_data" collection\ndb.students.aggregate([\n  {\n    $group: {\n      _id: "$class",\n      students: { $push: "$name" }\n    }\n  },\n  { $out: "class_data" }\n)\n\n// 2. $merge: Merge "city" and "phone" from "personal" collection into "students" on "_id"\ndb.personal.aggregate([\n  {\n    $merge: {\n      into: "students",\n      on: "_id",\n      whenMatched: "merge",\n      whenNotMatched: "insert"\n    }\n  }\n)\n\n// 3. $unionWith: Combine current students ("students1") and alumni ("students2") in a single query\ndb.students1.aggregate([\n  {\n    $unionWith: {\n      coll: "students2"\n    }\n  }\n)\n```	Yahoo Baba	https://www.youtube.com/@YahooBaba	655	Lecture 21: Cross-Collection Pipeline Stages — $out, $merge & $unionWith	Materialize aggregation results into new collections using $out, incrementally merge or upsert pipeline outputs into existing collections with $merge, and combine multi-collection datasets on read with $unionWith.	20	Easy	\N	21	[{"id": "mongo-21-prob-1", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bf7a3fe74e0db3762d", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bf7a3fe74e0db3762d", "name": "Problem #118: Find all reviews", "title": "Problem #118: Find all reviews", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "118", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Return all documents from **reviews**.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bf7a3fe74e0db3762d"}, {"id": "mongo-21-prob-2", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bf7a3fe74e0db3762a", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bf7a3fe74e0db3762a", "name": "Proble