wn independent array of pipeline stages on the same input documents and outputs its results as a dedicated array in a single combined response document.\n\n### 💡 Imputing Missing / Null Values with `$fill`\n* **Constant Value Fill:** `output: { per: { value: 0 } }` replaces any missing or `null` `per` field with `0`. (Note: specify either `value` OR `method`, never both together).\n* **Last Observation Carried Forward (`method: "locf"`):** `output: { per: { method: "locf" } }` fills a missing value with the value from the immediately preceding document.\n* **Linear Interpolation (`method: "linear"`):** Calculates the midpoint between the preceding document's value and the following document's value (e.g., between `83` and `77` -> fills `80`). **Requires `sortBy`** inside `$fill`.\n* **`partitionBy` (Optional):** Partitions documents into independent groups (e.g., `partitionBy: { class: "$class" }`) before applying `locf` or `linear` filling.\n\n### 🛠️ Practical $facet & $fill Examples\n```javascript\n// 1. $facet: Compute Top 3 Products, Total Revenue, and Sales by Region in 1 query\ndb.sales.aggregate([\n  {\n    $facet: {\n      topProducts: [\n        {\n          $group: {\n            _id: "$product",\n            totalSales: { $sum: { $multiply: ["$price", "$quantity" } }\n          }\n        },\n        { $sort: { totalSales: -1 } },\n        { $limit: 3 }\n      ,\n      totalRevenue: [\n        {\n          $group: {\n            _id: null,\n            totalRevenue: { $sum: { $multiply: ["$price", "$quantity" } }\n          }\n        }\n      ,\n      salesByRegion: [\n        {\n          $group: {\n            _id: "$region",\n            count: { $sum: 1 }\n          }\n        },\n        { $sort: { count: -1 } }\n      \n    }\n  }\n)\n\n// 2. $fill with a constant default value (0)\ndb.students.aggregate([\n  {\n    $fill: {\n      output: {\n        per: { value: 0 }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n)\n\n// 3. $fill with linear interpolation partitioned by class and sorted by _id\ndb.students.aggregate([\n  {\n    $fill: {\n      partitionBy: { class: "$class" },\n      sortBy: { _id: 1 },\n      output: {\n        per: { method: "linear" }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n)\n```	Yahoo Baba	https://www.youtube.com/@YahooBaba	655	Lecture 22: Multi-Faceted Aggregations & Missing Data Imputation — $facet & $fill	Execute multiple independent aggregation sub-pipelines in a single database query using $facet, and impute missing or null field values using $fill (constant value, locf, and linear interpolation).	20	Easy	\N	22	[{"id": "mongo-22-prob-1", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bf7a3fe74e0db37648", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bf7a3fe74e0db37648", "name": "Problem #109: Find reviews with rating 1", "title": "Problem #109: Find reviews with rating 1", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "109", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Return reviews where **rating** is 1.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bf7a3fe74e0db37648"}, {"id": "mongo-22-prob-2", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bf7a3fe74e0db37642", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bf7a3fe74e0db37642", "name": "Problem #111: Find discontinued inventory", "title": "Problem #111: Find discontinued inventory", "platform": "MongoPractice", "problemId": "111", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Return inventory where **discontinued** is true.", "external_url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bf7a3fe74e0db37642"}, {"id": "mongo-22-prob-3", "url": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bf7a3fe74e0db3763f", "link": "https://mongopractice.online/mongodb-practice-questions/69aab9bf7a3fe74e0db3763f", "name": "Problem #112: Find non discontinued inventory", "title": "Problem #112: Find non discontinued inventory", "platform": "Mongo