ader("Content-Type", "text/html");\n  res.write("<html><body><h1>Like / Share / Subscribe</h1></body></html>");\n  res.end();\n});\n\nserver.listen(3001);\n```	Complete Coding by Prashant Sir	https://www.youtube.com/@CompleteCodingByPrashantSir	24	Lecture 4: Request & Response Lifecycle — Inspecting req (url, method, headers), Sending HTML via res, URL Routing & 302 Redirects	Inspect incoming HTTP requests (req.url, req.method, req.headers), construct HTML responses using res.setHeader, res.write, and res.end, implement multi-page routing, and trigger 302 redirects.	20	Easy	\N	4	[{"id": "node-lec-4-q1", "url": null, "link": null, "name": "Q1: Why do we get the error \\"Cannot set headers after they are sent to the client\\" (ERR_HTTP_HEADERS_SENT) in Node.js, and how do we prevent it?", "title": "Q1: Why do we get the error \\"Cannot set headers after they are sent to the client\\" (ERR_HTTP_HEADERS_SENT) in Node.js, and how do we prevent it?", "answer": "Once res.end() (or res.send() in Express) is called, the HTTP headers and response body are flushed over the TCP socket and the response is closed. However, calling res.end() does NOT automatically exit the JavaScript function! If an if (req.url === \\"/\\") block calls res.end() without a return statement (or without an else block), execution continues to the lines below and tries to call res.setHeader() or res.write() a second time on the same closed response. Always write return res.end(); to exit the callback immediately.", "platform": "Technical Interview QA", "problemId": "4-q1", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Once res.end() (or res.send() in Express) is called, the HTTP headers and response body are flushed over the TCP socket and the response is closed. However, calling res.end() does NOT automatically exit the JavaScript function! If an if (req.url === \\"/\\") block calls res.end() without a return statement (or without an else block), execution continues to the lines below and tries to call res.