nd Strings", "HTML nodes and CSS variables"], "question": "What two types of data structures can the `use` hook consume?", "explanation": "The `use` hook is designed to read the value of a Promise (suspending the component until resolved) or read a Context value dynamically.", "correctAnswer": "B", "correct_index": 1, "correct_answer": "Promises and Context objects"}, {"id": 3, "type": "multiple_choice", "answer": "B", "options": ["It prevents Suspense from rendering", "If `use` receives a pending Promise, it suspends the component rendering and triggers the nearest `<Suspense>` boundary fallback", "It renders the Promise as a string while waiting", "It automatically caches the Suspense boundary"], "question": "How does the `use` hook integrate with React `<Suspense>`?", "explanation": "When reading a Promise via `use()`, React will natively pause the component's render cycle and display the fallback UI until the Promise resolves.", "correctAnswer": "B", "correct_index": 1, "correct_answer": "If `use` receives a pending Promise, it suspends the component rendering and triggers the nearest `<Suspense>` boundary fallback"}]	\N	> **Architectural Deep Dive:** This lecture covers the strict technical nuances, reconciliation behavior, and performance implications of using use in production environments. Pay special attention to concurrent rendering behaviors in React 18+.	Web Dev Simplified	https://www.youtube.com/@WebDevSimplified	\N	This New React Hook Breaks All The Rules (use)	Deep dive architectural lecture focusing on the mechanics, use cases, and anti-patterns of the use hook.	15	Easy	Core Hooks & API	16	[]	\N	15	https://youtu.be/zdNF9FJWJ8o	This New React Hook Breaks All The Rules (use)
