22074	Lecture 16: Fixing pgAdmin 4 UI Lag — Running pgAdmin in Browser Mode via Application Server URL	pg-lecture-16-pgadmin4-browser-performance-optimization	Resolve desktop UI lag on macOS (M1/M2/M3) and Windows by running pgAdmin 4 directly inside Chrome/Brave via the local Application Server URL.	2026-10-05 19:34:44.247876+05:30	### 🎯 Engineering Guide: Lecture 16: Fixing pgAdmin 4 UI Lag — Running pgAdmin in Browser Mode via Application Server URL\nPart of the **PostgreSQL & Relational SQL Mastery** curriculum designed for modern software development.\n\n- **Core Concepts**: Architectural patterns, modular design principles, and production best practices.\n- **Hands-on Objective**: Understand the lifecycle, error boundaries, and integration points with the rest of the application stack.\n- **Production Checklist**:\n  - Clean separation of concerns (controller, service, repository layers).\n  - Robust error handling and structured logging.\n  - Unit and integration testing considerations.	[{"url": "https://developer.mozilla.org/", "title": "MDN Web Docs"}, {"url": "https://devdocs.io/", "title": "Official Documentation & API Reference"}]	[{"url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IIMOXsHWYjA", "title": "Why pgAdmin 4 is So Slow on Mac M1/M2/M3 Pro (And How to Fix It)", "duration": "4m", "creator_name": "Thapa Technical (Vinod Bahadur Thapa)", "creator_channel_url": "https://www.youtube.com/@ThapaTechnical"}]	[{"id": "pg-16-prob-1", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/recyclable-and-low-fat-products/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/recyclable-and-low-fat-products/", "name": "Recyclable and Low Fat Products", "title": "Recyclable and Low Fat Products", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "16_1", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Solve \\"Recyclable and Low Fat Products\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/recyclable-and-low-fat-products/"}, {"id": "pg-16-prob-2", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/fin