-prob-7", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/customers-who-never-order/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/customers-who-never-order/", "name": "Customers Who Never Order", "title": "Customers Who Never Order", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "16_7", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Solve \\"Customers Who Never Order\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/customers-who-never-order/"}, {"id": "pg-16-prob-8", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/duplicate-emails/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/duplicate-emails/", "name": "Duplicate Emails", "title": "Duplicate Emails", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "16_8", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Solve \\"Duplicate Emails\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/duplicate-emails/"}, {"id": "pg-16-prob-9", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/employees-earning-more-than-their-managers/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/employees-earning-more-than-their-managers/", "name": "Employees Earning More Than Their Managers", "title": "Employees Earning More Than Their Managers", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "16_9", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Solve \\"Employees Earning More Than Their Managers\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/employees-earning-more-than-their-managers/"}, {"id": "pg-16-prob-10", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/delete-duplicate-emails/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/delete-duplicate-emails/", "name": "Delete Duplicate Emails", "title": "Delete Duplicate Emails", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "16_10", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Solve \\"Delete Duplicate Emails\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/delete-duplicate-emails/"}]	\N	### 📌 Topic Overview\nThe standalone **pgAdmin 4** desktop application runs inside an embedded web wrapper that frequently suffers from 5–10 second input lag (especially on Apple Silicon M1/M2/M3 Macs and high-DPI monitors). Because pgAdmin 4 is architected as a local Python web server, you can bypass the sluggish desktop wrapper and run it at 60 FPS directly inside your web browser.\n\n### ⚡ Step-by-Step Fix: Running pgAdmin 4 in Your Browser\n\n1. **Launch the pgAdmin 4 Desktop App:** Let the application finish its initial startup sequence.\n2. **Open the Server Logs:**\n   * Click the **pgAdmin 4** menu (top-left menu bar on macOS or system tray icon) -> Select **View Logs**.\n3. **Copy the Local Application Server URL:**\n   * Scroll to the bottom of the log window and copy the **Application Server URL** (e.g., `http://127.0.0.1:xxxxx/?key=...`).\n4. **Paste into Chrome / Brave / Edge:**\n   * Open your browser, paste the URL, and press Enter. The Query Tool, Object Explorer, and data grids will now respond instantaneously.\n\n### ⚠️ Critical Rule: Keep the Desktop App Running in the Background\n* **Do NOT Quit (`Cmd + Q` / `Alt + F4`) the pgAdmin 4 Desktop App** while working in the browser.\n* The desktop app hosts the local background server daemon and session token. Quitting the desktop app terminates the local server and triggers a `Connection Lost` error in your browser tab. Simply minimize it to the background.	Thapa Technical (Vinod Bahadur Thapa)	https://www.youtube.com/@ThapaTechnical	654	Lecture 16: Fixing pgAdmin 4 UI Lag — Running pgAdmin in Browser Mode via Application Server URL	Resolve desktop UI lag on macOS (M1/M2/M3) and Windows by running pgAdmin 4 directly inside Chrome/Brave via the local Application Server URL.	4	Easy	Module 1: PostgreSQL Foundations & Setup	16	[{"id": "pg-16-prob-1", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/recyclable-and-low-fat-products/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/recyclable-and-low-fat-products/", "name": "Recyclable and Low Fat Products", "title": "Recyclable and Low Fat Products", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "16_1"