1114	Value-Range Binary Search & Upper-Bound Counting: Median in a Row-Wise Sorted Matrix	dsa-median-in-row-wise-sorted-matrix	Find the median of an N x M row-wise sorted matrix in O(log(max - min) * N * log M) time using upper-bound binary search on value range.	2026-10-03 00:35:47.104972+05:30	### 🎯 Algorithmic Pattern Breakdown: Value-Range Binary Search & Upper-Bound Counting: Median in a Row-Wise Sorted Matrix\nMastering this module is critical for technical coding rounds and LeetCode algorithmic interviews.\n\n- **Core Problem-Solving Pattern**: Break down problem constraints, identify edge cases (empty inputs, negative values, integer overflow), and establish time/space complexity bounds.\n- **Optimal Complexity Target**: Aim for O(N) or O(N log N) time complexity with O(1) or O(N) auxiliary space.\n- **Interview Walkthrough Strategy**:\n  1. Clarify inputs, outputs, and constraints before coding.\n  2. State brute force approach and explain why it is sub-optimal.\n  3. Walk the interviewer through the optimized algorithm with a small test case.\n  4. Write clean, modular code with descriptive variable names.	[{"url": "https://neetcode.io/roadmap", "title": "NeetCode Algorithmic Roadmap"}, {"url": "https://leetcode.com/problemset/all/", "title": "LeetCode Problem Set"}]	[{"url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Q9wXgdxJq48", "title": "Lecture 72: Median in a Row-Wise Sorted Matrix", "duration": "32m"}]	[{"url": "https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/median-in-a-row-wise-sorted-matrix1527/1", "title": "Median in a row-wise sorted Matrix", "platform": "GeeksforGeeks", "difficulty": "Hard", "description": "Find the median of an N x M row-wise sorted matrix where N and M are odd."}, {"url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/kth-smallest-element-in-a-sorted-matrix/", "title": "Kth Smallest Element in a Sorted Matrix", "platform": "LeetCode", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Use value-range binary search to count elements <= mid across sorted rows."}, {"url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/kth-smallest-number-in-multiplication-table/", "title": "Kth Smallest Number in Multiplication Table", "platform": "LeetCode", "difficulty": "Hard", "description": "Binary search on the value range while counting row elements <= mid."}]	Module 14: Multi-Array Partitioning & 2D Matrix Binary Search	### 📌 Topic Overview\nGiven an `N x M` matrix where `N` and `M` are both odd and every row is sorted individually, find the overall **median** in `O(log2(max - min) * N * log2 M)` time without flattening the matrix.\n\n### 💡 Key Takeaways\n- **The Median Property:**\n  - Since `N * M` is odd, the median has `req = (N * M) / 2` elements on its left and `req` elements on its right.\n  - The median is the **first number `x`** for which the total count of matrix elements `<= x` is **strictly greater than `req`** (`countSmallEqual(x) > (N * M) / 2`)!\n- **Counting Elements `<= mid` Using Upper Bound (`O(N * log2 M)`):**\n  - Because each row is sorted, the count of elements `<= mid` in row `i` is simply the **Upper Bound index of `mid`** in `matrix[i]`!\n- **Binary Search on Value Space:**\n  - Set `low` to the minimum element in column `0` and `high` to the maximum element in column `M - 1`.\n  - If `countSmallEqual(mat, mid) <= req`, we need a larger value (`low = mid + 1`).\n  - Otherwise, try a smaller value (`high = mid - 1`).\n  - Return `low`.\n\n### 💻 Matrix Median Blueprint\n```cpp\nint countSmallEqual(vector<vector<int>> &mat, int x) {\n    int cnt = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < mat.size(); i++) {\n        cnt += upper_bound(mat[i].begin(), mat[i].end(), x) - mat[i].begin();\n    }\n    return cnt;\n}\n\nint matrixMedian(vector<vector<int>> &mat) {\n    int n = mat.size(), m = mat[0].size();\n    int low = INT_MAX, high = INT_MIN;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        low = min(low, mat[i][0]);\n        high = max(high, mat[i][m - 1]);\n    }\n    int req = (n * m) / 2;\n    while (low <= high) {\n        int mid = low + (high - low) / 2;\n        if (countSmallEqual(mat, mid) <= req) low = mid + 1;\n        else high = mid - 1;\n    }\n    return low;\n}\n```	take U forward (Striver)	https://www.youtube.com/@takeUforward	25	\N	\N	20	Easy	\N	1	[]	\N	\N	\N	\N
