s-and-examinations/"}, {"id": "pg-22-prob-2", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/project-employees-i/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/project-employees-i/", "name": "Project Employees I (JOIN + GROUP BY + ROUND AVG)", "title": "Project Employees I (JOIN + GROUP BY + ROUND AVG)", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "22_2", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Solve \\"Project Employees I (JOIN + GROUP BY + ROUND AVG)\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/project-employees-i/"}, {"id": "pg-22-prob-3", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/average-selling-price/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/average-selling-price/", "name": "Average Selling Price (JOIN + GROUP BY + ROUND)", "title": "Average Selling Price (JOIN + GROUP BY + ROUND)", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "22_3", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Solve \\"Average Selling Price (JOIN + GROUP BY + ROUND)\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/average-selling-price/"}, {"id": "pg-22-prob-4", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/the-number-of-employees-which-report-to-each-employee/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/the-number-of-employees-which-report-to-each-employee/", "name": "The Number of Employees Which Report to Each Employee (JOIN + GROUP BY + ROUND AVG)", "title": "The Number of Employees Which Report to Each Employee (JOIN + GROUP BY + ROUND AVG)", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "22_4", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Solve \\"The Number of Employees Which Report to Each Employee (JOIN + GROUP BY + ROUND AVG)\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/the-number-of-employees-which-report-to-each-employee/"}, {"id": "pg-22-prob-5", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/confirmation-rate/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/confirmation-rate/", "name": "Confirmation Rate", "title": "Confirmation Rate", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "22_5", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Solve \\"Confirmation Rate\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/confirmation-rate/"}, {"id": "pg-22-prob-6", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/department-highest-salary/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/department-highest-salary/", "name": "Department Highest Salary", "title": "Department Highest Salary", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "22_6", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Solve \\"Department Highest Salary\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/department-highest-salary/"}, {"id": "pg-22-prob-7", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/monthly-transactions-i/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/monthly-transactions-i/", "name": "Monthly Transactions I", "title": "Monthly Transactions I", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "22_7", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Solve \\"Monthly Transactions I\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/monthly-transactions-i/"}, {"id": "pg-22-prob-8", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/restaurant-growth/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/restaurant-growth/", "name": "Restaurant Growth", "title": "Restaurant Growth", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "22_8", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Solve \\"Restaurant Growth\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/restaurant-growth/"}, {"id": "pg-22-prob-9", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/department-top-three-salaries/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/department-top-three-salaries/", "name": "Department Top Three Salaries", "title": "Department Top Three Salaries", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "22_9", "difficulty": "Hard", "description": "Solve \\"Department Top Three Salaries\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/department-top-three-salaries/"}, {"id": "pg-22-prob-10", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/human-traffic-of-stadium/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/human-traffic-of-stadium/", "name": "Human Traffic of Stadium", "title": "Human Traffic of Stadium", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "22_10", "difficulty": "Hard", "description": "Solve \\"Human Traffic of Stadium\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/human-traffic-of-stadium/"}]	\N	### 📌 Topic Overview\nThis lecture solves the two remaining multi-table analytical challenges from Part 1, demonstrating how to chain **3-table `INNER JOIN`s** with **multi-column `GROUP BY`**, **`HAVING`**, and **`ROUND(AVG(...), 2)`**.\n\n### 🏆 Challenge 2: Popular Premium Courses (3-Table Join)\n\n#### Business Requirement:\nIdentify which expensive courses are actually popular so the college can award bonuses to the teaching professors:\n* Display the **course title**, **professor name**, and **total number of enrolled students**.\n* **Filter 1 (Row-level):** Only include premium courses where `fee > 3000`.\n* **Filter 2 (Group-level):** Only include courses that have **at least 2 enrolled students** (`>= 2`).\n* **Sorting:** Sort by total enrolled students descending.\n\n```sql\nSELECT \n    c.title AS course_title,\n    u.name AS professor_name,\n    COUNT(e.student_id) AS total_students\nFROM courses c\nINNER JOIN users u\n    ON c.instructor_id = u.id\nINNER JOIN enrollments e\n    ON c.id = e.course_id\nWHERE c.fee > 3000\nGROUP BY c.title, u.name\nHAVING COUNT(e.student_id) >= 2\nORDER BY total_students DESC;\n```\n*(Note: Because both `c.title` and `u.name` appear in `SELECT` outside of `COUNT()`, both must be listed in `GROUP BY c.title, u.name`)*.\n\n### 🏆 Challenge 3: The Department Budget Audit (`ROUND(AVG(), 2)`)\n\n#### Business Requirement:\nThe finance department is auditing the average course fee across departments taught by active professors:\n* Calculate the **average course fee per department**, rounded to **2 decimal places**.\n* **Filter 1 (Row-level):** Only include courses taught by professors who are currently active (`u.is_active = true`).\n* **Filter 2 (Group-level):** Only show affordable departments where the average course fee is strictly less than `4000`.\n* **Sorting:** Sort from cheapest to most expensive (`ASC`).\n\n```sql\nSELECT \n    d.name AS department_name,\n    ROUND(AVG(c.fee), 2) AS avg_course_fee\nFROM departments d\nINNER JOIN users u\n    ON d.id = u.department_id\nINNER JOIN courses c\n    ON u.id = c.instructor_id\nWHERE u.is_active = true\nGROUP BY d.name\nHAVING AVG(c.fee) < 4000\nORDER BY avg_course_fee ASC;\n```	Thapa Technical (Vinod Bahadur Thapa)	https://www.youtube.com/@ThapaTechnical	654	Lecture 22: Advanced SQL Interview Practice (Part 2) — 3-Table Joins with GROUP BY, HAVING & ROUND(AVG)	Master 3-table relational hops (courses -> users -> enrollments and departments -> users -> courses) combined with multi-column GROUP BY and HAVING.	11	Medium	Module 6: Aggregations, Grouping & Analytical Queries	22	[{"id": "pg-22-prob-1", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/students-and-examinations/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/students-and-examinations/", "name": "Students and Examinations (3-Table Join + GROUP BY)", "title": "Students and Examinations (3-Table Join + GROUP BY)", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "22_1", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Solve \\"Students and Examinations (3-Table Join + GROUP BY)\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/students-and-examinations/"}, {"id": "pg-22-prob-2", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/project-employees-i/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/project-employees-i/", "name": "Project Employees I (JOIN + GROUP BY + ROUND AVG)", "title": "Project Employees I (JOIN + GROUP BY + ROUND AVG)", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "22_2", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Solve \\"Project Employees