/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/find-customer-referee/", "name": "Find Customer Referee", "title": "Find Customer Referee", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "3_2", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Solve \\"Find Customer Referee\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/find-customer-referee/"}, {"id": "pg-3-prob-3", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/big-countries/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/big-countries/", "name": "Big Countries", "title": "Big Countries", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "3_3", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Solve \\"Big Countries\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/big-countries/"}, {"id": "pg-3-prob-4", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/article-views-i/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/article-views-i/", "name": "Article Views I", "title": "Article Views I", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "3_4", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Solve \\"Article Views I\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/article-views-i/"}, {"id": "pg-3-prob-5", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/invalid-tweets/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/invalid-tweets/", "name": "Invalid Tweets", "title": "Invalid Tweets", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "3_5", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Solve \\"Invalid Tweets\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/invalid-tweets/"}, {"id": "pg-3-prob-6", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/combine-two-tables/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/combine-two-tables/", "name": "Combine Two Tables", "title": "Combine Two Tables", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "3_6", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Solve \\"Combine Two Tables\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/combine-two-tables/"}, {"id": "pg-3-prob-7", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/customers-who-never-order/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/customers-who-never-order/", "name": "Customers Who Never Order", "title": "Customers Who Never Order", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "3_7", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Solve \\"Customers Who Never Order\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/customers-who-never-order/"}, {"id": "pg-3-prob-8", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/duplicate-emails/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/duplicate-emails/", "name": "Duplicate Emails", "title": "Duplicate Emails", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "3_8", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Solve \\"Duplicate Emails\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/duplicate-emails/"}, {"id": "pg-3-prob-9", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/employees-earning-more-than-their-managers/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/employees-earning-more-than-their-managers/", "name": "Employees Earning More Than Their Managers", "title": "Employees Earning More Than Their Managers", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "3_9", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Solve \\"Employees Earning More Than Their Managers\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/employees-earning-more-than-their-managers/"}, {"id": "pg-3-prob-10", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/delete-duplicate-emails/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/delete-duplicate-emails/", "name": "Delete Duplicate Emails", "title": "Delete Duplicate Emails", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "3_10", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Solve \\"Delete Duplicate Emails\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/delete-duplicate-emails/"}]	\N	### 📌 Topic Overview\nThis lecture covers **Data Definition Language (DDL)** fundamentals: creating and dropping databases and tables via both the `psql` CLI and the **pgAdmin 4 Query Tool**, along with essential PostgreSQL naming and quoting rules.\n\n### 💻 Essential `psql` CLI Meta-Commands vs. SQL Queries\nNote that backslash commands (`\\l`, `\\c`, `\\dt`) are **CLI-only meta-commands** and will throw syntax errors inside the pgAdmin 4 Query Tool.\n\n* **List All Databases:** `\\l` — `SELECT datname FROM pg_database;`\n* **Connect / Switch Database:** `\\c college_management` — *(Click database in pgAdmin Object Explorer)*\n* **Check Active Database:** `\\conninfo` — `SELECT current_database();`\n* **List Tables in Public Schema:** `\\dt` — `SELECT * FROM pg_tables WHERE schemaname = 'public';`\n\n### 🗄️ Creating & Dropping Databases and Tables\n\n```sql\n-- 1. Create a new database\nCREATE DATABASE college_management;\n\n-- 2. Drop a database safely (Note: cannot drop if another session is actively connected)\nDROP DATABASE IF EXISTS testing;\n\n-- 3. Create a table with proper data types & constraints\nCREATE TABLE users (\n    id SERIAL PRIMARY KEY,\n    name VARCHAR(100),\n    email VARCHAR(100),\n    is_active BOOLEAN\n);\n\n-- 4. Practice Task: Create the courses table with exact decimal precision\nCREATE TABLE courses (\n    id SERIAL PRIMARY KEY,\n    title VARCHAR(150),\n    fee NUMERIC(10, 2)\n);\n```\n\n### ⚠️ Critical PostgreSQL Best Practices & Common Pitfalls\n\n1. **Single Quotes vs. Double Quotes (Crucial Difference from MySQL):**\n   * **Single Quotes (`'public'`):** Used strictly for **string values/literals**.\n   * **Double Quotes (`"public"`):** Used strictly for **identifiers** (table names or column names). Writing `WHERE schemaname = "public"` fails with `ERROR: column "public" does not exist`.\n2. **No Trailing Comma on the Final Column:** Including a comma after the last column definition inside `CREATE TABLE (...)` throws a syntax error.\n3. **Right-Size `VARCHAR(n)`:** Avoid blindly setting `VARCHAR(255)` for short strings like phone numbers (`VARCHAR(20)` is sufficient).\n4. **Naming Conventions:** Use uppercase for SQL keywords (`CREATE TABLE`, `SELECT`, `WHERE`) and `snake_case` plural nouns for table names (`users`, `courses`, `departments`).	Thapa Technical (Vinod Bahadur Thapa)	https://www.youtube.com/@ThapaTechnical	654	Lecture 3: Creating Databases & Tables — DDL Syntax, Data Types & psql Meta-Commands	Create and drop databases and tables using both psql CLI and pgAdmin 4 Query Tool, master single vs double quotes, and query pg_tables metadata.	27	Easy	Module 1: PostgreSQL Foundations & Setup	3	[{"id": "pg-3-prob-1", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/recyclable-and-low-fat-products/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/recyclable-and-low-fat-products/", "name": "Recyclable and Low Fat Products", "title": "Recyclable and Low Fat Products", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "3_1", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Solve \\"Recyclable and Low Fat Products\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/recyclable-and-low-fat-products/"}, {"id": "pg-3-prob-2", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/find-customer-referee/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/find-customer-referee/", "name": "Find Customer Referee", "title": "Find Customer Referee", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "3_2", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Solve \\"Find Customer Referee\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/find-customer-referee/"}, {"id": "pg-3-prob-3", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/big-countries/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/big-countries/", "name": "Big Countries", "title": "Big Countries", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "3_3", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Solve \\"Big Countries\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/big-countries/"}, {"id": "pg-3-prob-4", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/article-views-i/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/article-views-i/", "name": "Art