ternal_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/sales-analysis-iii/"}, {"id": "pg-9-prob-6", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/fix-names-in-a-table/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/fix-names-in-a-table/", "name": "Fix Names in a Table", "title": "Fix Names in a Table", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "9_6", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Solve \\"Fix Names in a Table\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/fix-names-in-a-table/"}, {"id": "pg-9-prob-7", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/group-sold-products-by-the-date/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/group-sold-products-by-the-date/", "name": "Group Sold Products By The Date", "title": "Group Sold Products By The Date", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "9_7", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Solve \\"Group Sold Products By The Date\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/group-sold-products-by-the-date/"}, {"id": "pg-9-prob-8", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/tree-node/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/tree-node/", "name": "Tree Node (IN Clause Filtering)", "title": "Tree Node (IN Clause Filtering)", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "9_8", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Solve \\"Tree Node (IN Clause Filtering)\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/tree-node/"}, {"id": "pg-9-prob-9", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/department-highest-salary/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/department-highest-salary/", "name": "Department Highest Salary (IN Tuple Matching)", "title": "Department Highest Salary (IN Tuple Matching)", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "9_9", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Solve \\"Department Highest Salary (IN Tuple Matching)\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/department-highest-salary/"}, {"id": "pg-9-prob-10", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/investments-in-2016/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/investments-in-2016/", "name": "Investments in 2016 (IN / NOT IN Filtering)", "title": "Investments in 2016 (IN / NOT IN Filtering)", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "9_10", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Solve \\"Investments in 2016 (IN / NOT IN Filtering)\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/investments-in-2016/"}]	\N	### 📌 Topic Overview\nPostgreSQL provides four specialized filtering operators—**`IN`**, **`BETWEEN`**, **`LIKE`**, and **`ILIKE`**—that make complex `WHERE` clauses cleaner, more readable, and ideal for search bars and range filters.\n\n### 🛠️ 1. The `IN` Operator (Clean Alternative to Multiple `OR`s)\nMatches a column against a comma-separated list of values:\n```sql\n-- Instead of: WHERE department_id = 2 OR department_id = 4 OR department_id = 5\nSELECT name, email, department_id\nFROM users\nWHERE department_id IN (2, 4, 5);\n```\n*(Note: Never write `WHERE id = (2, 4, 5)` — `=` cannot compare against a list).*\n\n### 📏 2. The `BETWEEN` Operator (Inclusive Ranges)\n`BETWEEN low AND high` is **inclusive** of both endpoints (`>= low AND <= high`):\n```sql\n-- Includes courses priced at exactly 2500 and 4000\nSELECT title, fee\nFROM courses\nWHERE fee BETWEEN 2500 AND 4000;\n```\n*(If you need an exclusive range that omits 2500 and 4000, use `WHERE fee > 2500 AND fee < 4000` instead).*\n\n### 🔎 3. Pattern Matching: `LIKE` vs. `ILIKE` & Wildcards\n\n* **`LIKE`:** **Case-sensitive** pattern match. — `name LIKE '%Sharma%'` (Matches `'Sharma'`, ignores `'sharma'`)\n* **`ILIKE`:** **Case-insensitive** match (PostgreSQL extension, ideal for UI search bars). — `name ILIKE '%thapa%'` (Matches `'Thapa'`, `'THAPA'`, `'thapa'`)\n* **`%` Wildcard:** Matches **0 or more** characters. — `'A%'` matches `'A'`, `'Aman'`, `'Abhishek'`.\n* **`_` Wildcard:** Matches **exactly 1** character. — `'A___'` matches 4-letter names starting with A (e.g., `'Aman'`).\n\n```sql\n-- UI Search Bar Query (Case-Insensitive)\nSELECT id, name, email\nFROM users\nWHERE name ILIKE '%thapa%';\n```\n\n* **Note:** **Performance Warning (Leading Wildcards):** Writing `ILIKE '%sharma%'` with a leading `%` forces PostgreSQL to scan every row one-by-one (Sequential Scan), bypassing standard B-Tree indexes.	Thapa Technical (Vinod Bahadur Thapa)	https://www.youtube.com/@ThapaTechnical	654	Lecture 9: Advanced Filtering — IN, BETWEEN, LIKE & ILIKE Pattern Matching	Write concise set filters with IN, inclusive range checks with BETWEEN, and wildcard text searches using LIKE, ILIKE, % and _.	22	Easy	Module 3: Filtering, Pattern Matching & Pagination	9	[{"id": "pg-9-prob-1", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/patients-with-a-condition/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/patients-with-a-condition/", "name": "Patients With a Condition (LIKE Pattern Matching)", "title": "Patients With a Condition (LIKE Pattern Matching)", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "9_1", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Solve \\"Patients With a Condition (LIKE Pattern Matching)\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/patients-with-a-condition/"}, {"id": "pg-9-prob-2", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/find-users-with-valid-e-mails/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/find-users-with-valid-e-mails/", "name": "Find Users With Valid E-Mails (String Pattern Matching)", "title": "Find Users With Valid E-Mails (String Pattern Matching)", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "9_2", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Solve \\"Find Users With Valid E-Mails (String Pattern Matching)\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/find-users-with-valid-e-mails/"}, {"id": "pg-9-prob-3", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/list-the-products-ordered-in-a-period/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/list-the-products-ordered-in-a-period/", "name": "List the Products