1651	Recursive Divergence Point: Lowest Common Ancestor (LCA) in a Binary Tree	dsa-lowest-common-ancestor-binary-tree	Identify the lowest common ancestor of two nodes in O(N) time and O(H) space using single-pass bottom-up DFS divergence.	2026-10-03 01:02:00.07982+05:30	### 🎯 Algorithmic Pattern Breakdown: Recursive Divergence Point: Lowest Common Ancestor (LCA) in a Binary Tree\nMastering this module is critical for technical coding rounds and LeetCode algorithmic interviews.\n\n- **Core Problem-Solving Pattern**: Break down problem constraints, identify edge cases (empty inputs, negative values, integer overflow), and establish time/space complexity bounds.\n- **Optimal Complexity Target**: Aim for O(N) or O(N log N) time complexity with O(1) or O(N) auxiliary space.\n- **Interview Walkthrough Strategy**:\n  1. Clarify inputs, outputs, and constraints before coding.\n  2. State brute force approach and explain why it is sub-optimal.\n  3. Walk the interviewer through the optimized algorithm with a small test case.\n  4. Write clean, modular code with descriptive variable names.	[{"url": "https://neetcode.io/roadmap", "title": "NeetCode Algorithmic Roadmap"}, {"url": "https://leetcode.com/problemset/all/", "title": "LeetCode Problem Set"}]	[{"url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_-QHfMDde90", "title": "Lecture 99: Lowest Common Ancestor in Binary Tree", "duration": "25m"}]	[{"url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/lowest-common-ancestor-of-a-binary-tree/", "title": "Lowest Common Ancestor of a Binary Tree", "platform": "LeetCode", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Find the lowest common ancestor node of two given nodes in a binary tree."}, {"url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/lowest-common-ancestor-of-a-binary-search-tree/", "title": "Lowest Common Ancestor of a Binary Search Tree", "platform": "LeetCode", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Exploit BST key ordering to find LCA without searching both branches."}, {"url": "https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/lowest-common-ancestor-in-a-binary-tree/1", "title": "Lowest Common Ancestor in a Binary Tree", "platform": "GeeksforGeeks", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Find the LCA of two nodes in a binary tree in O(N) time and O(1) extra space."}]	Module 17: Binary Trees: Views, Projections & Ancestry Analysis	### 📌 Topic Overview\nThe **Lowest Common Ancestor (LCA)** of two nodes `p` and `q` is the deepest node in the tree that has both `p` and `q` as descendants (a node can be a descendant of itself).\n\n### 💡 Key Takeaways (Brute → Optimal)\n- **1. Brute Force via Root-to-Node Paths (`O(2N)` Time, `O(2N)` Space):**\n  - Find path 1 from root to `p` (`[1, 2, 4]`).\n  - Find path 2 from root to `q` (`[1, 2, 5, 7]`).\n  - Compare both paths from start to find the last common node (`2`).\n- **2. Optimal Single-Pass DFS (`O(N)` Time, `O(H)` Space):**\n  - Base Case: If `root == nullptr || root == p || root == q`, return `root`.\n  - Recurse left: `left = lowestCommonAncestor(root->left, p, q)`.\n  - Recurse right: `right = lowestCommonAncestor(root->right, p, q)`.\n  - **Divergence Rule:**\n    - If both `left != nullptr && right != nullptr`, one target was found in the left subtree and the other in the right subtree—**`root` is the LCA**!\n    - If `left == nullptr`, return `right` (both targets lie in the right branch).\n    - If `right == nullptr`, return `left`.\n\n### 💻 Lowest Common Ancestor Blueprint\n```cpp\nTreeNode* lowestCommonAncestor(TreeNode* root, TreeNode* p, TreeNode* q) {\n    if (root == nullptr || root == p || root == q) {\n        return root;\n    }\n    TreeNode* left = lowestCommonAncestor(root->left, p, q);\n    TreeNode* right = lowestCommonAncestor(root->right, p, q);\n\n    if (left == nullptr) return right;\n    else if (right == nullptr) return left;\n    else return root; // Both left and right returned non-null -> root is LCA!\n}\n```	take U forward (Striver)	https://www.youtube.com/@takeUforward	25	\N	\N	20	Easy	\N	1	[]	\N	\N	\N	