"LeetCode", "problemId": "15_5", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Solve \\"Average Time of Process per Machine (Self INNER JOIN)\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/average-time-of-process-per-machine/"}, {"id": "pg-15-prob-6", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/students-and-examinations/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/students-and-examinations/", "name": "Students and Examinations (3-Table Join)", "title": "Students and Examinations (3-Table Join)", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "15_6", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Solve \\"Students and Examinations (3-Table Join)\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/students-and-examinations/"}, {"id": "pg-15-prob-7", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/managers-with-at-least-5-direct-reports/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/managers-with-at-least-5-direct-reports/", "name": "Managers with at Least 5 Direct Reports (INNER JOIN + Aggregation)", "title": "Managers with at Least 5 Direct Reports (INNER JOIN + Aggregation)", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "15_7", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Solve \\"Managers with at Least 5 Direct Reports (INNER JOIN + Aggregation)\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/managers-with-at-least-5-direct-reports/"}, {"id": "pg-15-prob-8", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/department-highest-salary/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/department-highest-salary/", "name": "Department Highest Salary (INNER JOIN with Department)", "title": "Department Highest Salary (INNER JOIN with Department)", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "15_8", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Solve \\"Department Highest Salary (INNER JOIN with Department)\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/department-highest-salary/"}, {"id": "pg-15-prob-9", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/department-top-three-salaries/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/department-top-three-salaries/", "name": "Department Top Three Salaries", "title": "Department Top Three Salaries", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "15_9", "difficulty": "Hard", "description": "Solve \\"Department Top Three Salaries\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/department-top-three-salaries/"}, {"id": "pg-15-prob-10", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/tree-node/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/tree-node/", "name": "Tree Node", "title": "Tree Node", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "15_10", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Solve \\"Tree Node\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/tree-node/"}]	\N	### 📌 Topic Overview\nAn **`INNER JOIN`** represents the set intersection ($A \\cap B$) of two tables: it pairs rows from Table A and Table B where the `ON` condition matches, and **excludes any unmatched rows** from both sides.\n\n### 🔍 1. Two-Table `INNER JOIN` & Resolving Ambiguous Columns\nBoth `users` and `departments` have a column named `name`. Writing `SELECT name` throws `ERROR: column reference "name" is ambiguous`. Always prefix columns with their table name or **Table Alias**:\n\n```sql\n-- Fetch all professors along with their human-readable department name\nSELECT \n    u.name AS professor_name,\n    d.name AS department_name\nFROM users u\nINNER JOIN departments d\n    ON u.department_id = d.id\nWHERE u.role = 'professor';\n```\n\n### 🎓 2. Joining `users` & `courses` via Instructor Foreign Key\n```sql\n-- Find which professor is teaching which course and its fee\nSELECT \n    u.name AS instructor_name,\n    c.title AS course_title,\n    c.fee\nFROM users u\nINNER JOIN courses c\n    ON u.id = c.instructor_id;\n```\n\n### 🚀 3. The 3-Table Junction Join (`users` -> `enrollments` -> `courses`)\nTo display which student enrolled in which course, start at `users`, bridge through the `enrollments` junction table, and join `courses`:\n\n```sql\nSELECT \n    u.name AS student_name,\n    c.title AS course_title,\n    e.enrolled_on\nFROM users u\nINNER JOIN enrollments e\n    ON u.id = e.student_id\nINNER JOIN courses c\n    ON e.course_id = c.id;\n```\n\n### 💡 Senior Engineering Best Practices\n1. **Write `INNER JOIN` Explicitly:** While bare `JOIN` defaults to `INNER JOIN`, writing `INNER JOIN` makes your intent unmistakable against `LEFT JOIN` or `RIGHT JOIN`.\n2. **Unmatched Rows Are Filtered Out:** If a user has `department_id IS NULL`, they will **never** appear in an `INNER JOIN departments` result set.	Thapa Technical (Vinod Bahadur Thapa)	https://www.youtube.com/@ThapaTechnical	654	Lecture 15: Mastering INNER JOIN — Venn Diagrams, Table Aliases & 3-Table Junction Joins	Combine related tables using INNER JOIN, resolve ambiguous column names with table aliases, and write 3-table joins across users, enrollments, and courses.	20	Medium	Module 5: Relational Joins & Multi-Table Queries	15	[{"id": "pg-15-prob-1", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/replace-employee-id-with-the-unique-identifier/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/replace-employee-id-with-the-unique-identifier/", "name": "Replace Employee ID With The Unique Identifier", "title": "Replace Employee ID With The Unique Identifier", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "15_1", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Solve \\"Replace Employee ID With The Unique Identifier\\" on LeetCode using PostgreSQL.", "external_url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/replace-employee-id-with-the-unique-identifier/"}, {"id": "pg-15-prob-2", "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/product-sales-analysis-i/", "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/product-sales-analysis-i/", "name": "Product Sales Analysis I (INNER JOIN Basics)", "title": "Product Sales Analysis I (INNER JOIN Basics)", "platform": "LeetCode", "problemId": "15_2", "difficulty": "Easy", "description": "Solve \\"Produc