22266	Django + React Full Stack E-Commerce Build	django-react-ecommerce-full-stack	Build a production-ready e-commerce platform integrating Django REST Framework (DRF) backend, PostgreSQL, and a React frontend styled with TailwindCSS.	2026-10-11 22:46:20.744431+05:30	### 🎯 Engineering Guide: Django + React Full Stack E-Commerce Build\nPart of the **Development** curriculum designed for modern software development.\n\n- **Core Concepts**: Architectural patterns, modular design principles, and production best practices.\n- **Hands-on Objective**: Understand the lifecycle, error boundaries, and integration points with the rest of the application stack.\n- **Production Checklist**:\n  - Clean separation of concerns (controller, service, repository layers).\n  - Robust error handling and structured logging.\n  - Unit and integration testing considerations.	[{"url": "https://developer.mozilla.org/", "title": "MDN Web Docs"}, {"url": "https://devdocs.io/", "title": "Official Documentation & API Reference"}]	[{"url": "https://youtu.be/eeZDJCPTFx4", "title": "Django + React E-Commerce Full Stack Project | 3 Hours | Real World Project", "creator_name": "Mohit Decodes", "duration_minutes": 197, "creator_channel_url": "https://www.youtube.com/@mohitdecodes"}]	[{"id": "ec-1", "type": "quiz", "title": "Why is PostgreSQL preferred over SQLite for production E-Commerce apps?", "description": "PostgreSQL handles high concurrency, supports complex analytical queries, enforces strict data integrity, and does not suffer from SQLite's database-level locking during writes."}, {"id": "ec-2", "type": "quiz", "title": "How do you prevent a 'Race Condition' during checkout inventory deduction?", "description": "Use Django's `transaction.atomic()` combined with `select_for_update()` to lock the inventory row, ensuring concurrent checkout requests are processed sequentially."}, {"id": "ec-3", "type": "quiz", "title": "Why store JWT access tokens in memory and refresh tokens in HttpOnly cookies?", "description": "HttpOnly cookies mitigate Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) attacks because JavaScript cannot access them. In-memory access tokens protect against CSRF attacks."}, {"id": "ec-4", "type": "quiz", "title": "What is CORS and why must it be configured in a Django + React setup?", "description": "Cross-Origin Resource Sharing prevents browsers from making requests to a different domain/port. You must use `django-cors-headers` to whitelist the React app's URL."}, {"id": "ec-5", "type": "quiz", "title": "How do you optimize React Cart State management?", "description": "Use React Context API or Redux. Prevent unnecessary re-renders by using `useMemo` for derived data (like cart totals) and keeping the state shape normalized."}, {"id": "ec-6", "type": "quiz", "title": "Explain payment idempotency.", "description": "Idempotency ensures that making the same payment request multiple times (e.g., due to network drops) only charges the customer once, usually via unique Idempotency Keys."}, {"id": "ec-7", "type": "quiz", "title": "Why use TailwindCSS over traditional CSS frameworks in modern React apps?", "description": "Tailwind provides utility-first classes, enabling rapid styling without context switching to CSS files, and its build process purges unused CSS for extremely small bundle sizes."}, {"id": "ec-8", "type": "quiz", "title": "How do you handle API request authorization in React?", "description": "Create an Axios interceptor or a custom `authFetch` wrapper that automatically attaches the `Authorization: Bearer <token>` header to all outgoing requests."}, {"id": "ec-9", "type": "quiz", "title": "What is the purpose of `Vite` in modern React development?", "description": "Vite is a fast build tool and dev server that leverages native ES modules, providing instant hot module replacement (HMR) and significantly faster startup times than Webpack."}, {"id": "ec-10", "type": "quiz", "title": "How do you model an E-Commerce Cart in the database?", "description": "Typically requires two models: a `Cart` (linked to a User/Session) and `CartItem` (ForeignKeys to Cart and Product, plus Quantity). This handles many-to-many relationships."}, {"id": "ec-11", "type": "quiz", "title": "Why process image uploads asynchronously?", "description": "Image resizing and CDN uploading can take seconds, blocking the HTTP response. Offloading to Celery ensures the API responds immediately while processing happens in the background."}, {"id": "ec-12", "type": "quiz", "title": "How do you handle soft deletes for products?", "description": "Instead of hard deleting a product (which breaks old order history), add an `is_active` boolean field. Filter active products for the store, but keep inactive ones for historical records."}, {"id": "ec-13", "type": "quiz", "title": "Explain how to protect against Cart Abandonment.", "description": "Store cart data persistently in the database (or Redis) tied to the user session, rather than relying solely on local storage, allowing follow-up email campaigns."}, {"id": "ec-14", "type": "quiz", "title": "What is the `useEffect` cleanup function used for?", "description": "It prevents memory leaks by canceling active fetch requests, clearing timeouts/intervals, or unsubscribing from event listeners when a React component unmounts."}, {"id": "ec-15", "type": "quiz", "title": "How do you implement search functionality efficiently?", "description": "For simple searches, use Django's `icontains` filter. For production, integrate full-text search engines like PostgreSQL's `SearchVector` or external services like Elasticsearch/Algolia."}, {"id": "ec-16", "type": "quiz", "title": "Why use UUIDs for Order numbers instead of auto-incrementing integers?", "description": "Integer IDs expose your business metrics (competitors can guess order volume). UUIDs are unpredictable and non-sequential, providing better security and privacy."}, {"id": "ec-17", "type": "quiz", "title": "How do you manage environment-specific variables in React (Vite)?", "description": "Define variables in a `.env` file prefixed with `VITE_` (e.g., `VITE_API_BASE_URL`). Access them in code using `import.meta.env.VITE_API_BASE_URL`."}, {"id": "ec-18", "type": "quiz", "title": "What is the role of a DRF `ModelViewSet` in this project?", "description": "It drastically reduces boilerplate by automatically providing complete CRUD actions (list, create, retrieve, update, destroy) mapped to standard HTTP methods for a model."}, {"id": "ec-19", "type": "quiz", "title": "How do you handle JWT Token Expiration in the React frontend?", "description": "Implement an Axios interceptor that catches 401 Unauthorized errors. It should pause the original request, call the refresh token endpoint, update the access token, and retry the request."}, {"id": "ec-20", "type": "quiz", "title": "Why is database normalization important for an Order schema?", "description": "It reduces data redundancy. Storing historical snapshot data (like price at the time of purchase) in an `OrderItem` table prevents past orders from changing if the current product price changes."}]	\N	> **Note:** This practical build consolidates API design, React integration, and database architecture.\n\n### 📌 Architecture Breakdown\n1. **Infrastructure:** PostgreSQL database, DRF backend, and React (Vite) frontend.\n2. **CORS:** Enabling Cross-Origin Resource Sharing for backend-frontend communication.\n3. **Authentication:** JWT access and refresh token management stored securely.\n4. **State Management:** React Context API for global cart state and user session handling.\n5. **Checkout Flow:** Creating orders, handling quantities, and clearing cart data.	Mohit Decodes	https://www.youtube.com/@mohitdecodes	\N	Django + React Full Stack E-Commerce Build	Build a production-ready e-commerce platform integrating Django REST Framework (DRF) backend, PostgreSQL, and a React frontend styled with TailwindCSS.	197	Easy	Production Deployments & Integrations	2	[]	\N	197	https://youtu.be/eeZDJCPTFx4	Django + React E-Commerce Full Stack Project | 3 Hours | Real World Project
