956	Real-Valued Binary Search & Priority Queue Optimization: Minimise Maximum Distance to Gas Stations	dsa-minimise-maximum-distance-between-gas-stations	Minimize the maximum distance between adjacent gas stations within 10^-6 precision using real-valued binary search or max-heap greedy insertion.	2026-10-03 00:19:12.438247+05:30	### 🎯 Algorithmic Pattern Breakdown: Real-Valued Binary Search & Priority Queue Optimization: Minimise Maximum Distance to Gas Stations\nMastering this module is critical for technical coding rounds and LeetCode algorithmic interviews.\n\n- **Core Problem-Solving Pattern**: Break down problem constraints, identify edge cases (empty inputs, negative values, integer overflow), and establish time/space complexity bounds.\n- **Optimal Complexity Target**: Aim for O(N) or O(N log N) time complexity with O(1) or O(N) auxiliary space.\n- **Interview Walkthrough Strategy**:\n  1. Clarify inputs, outputs, and constraints before coding.\n  2. State brute force approach and explain why it is sub-optimal.\n  3. Walk the interviewer through the optimized algorithm with a small test case.\n  4. Write clean, modular code with descriptive variable names.	[{"url": "https://neetcode.io/roadmap", "title": "NeetCode Algorithmic Roadmap"}, {"url": "https://leetcode.com/problemset/all/", "title": "LeetCode Problem Set"}]	[{"url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kMSBvlZ-_HA", "title": "Lecture 64: Minimise Maximum Distance to Gas Station", "duration": "35m"}]	[{"url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/minimize-max-distance-to-gas-station/", "title": "Minimize Max Distance to Gas Station", "platform": "LeetCode", "difficulty": "Hard", "description": "Add k gas stations to minimize the maximum distance between adjacent stations with precision 10^-6."}, {"url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/koko-eating-bananas/", "title": "Koko Eating Bananas", "platform": "LeetCode", "difficulty": "Medium", "description": "Binary search on integer eating speeds to satisfy hour constraints."}, {"url": "https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/minimize-max-distance-to-gas-station/1", "title": "Minimize Max Distance to Gas Station", "platform": "GeeksforGeeks", "difficulty": "Hard", "description": "Add k stations along a road to minimize the maximum segment distance."}]	Module 13: Binary Search on Answer Space & Monotonic Predicate Functions	### 📌 Topic Overview\nGiven `n` gas station coordinates and an integer `k`, place `k` new gas stations between existing ones so that the **maximum distance between adjacent stations is minimized**. The answer must be accurate within `10^-6`.\n\n### 💡 Key Takeaways\n- **Heap Approach (Better — O(K log N) Time, O(N) Space):**\n  - Use a max-heap (`priority_queue`) to greedily find the section with the largest distance and insert a gas station there.\n- **Binary Search on Real Values (Optimal — O(N * log((maxDist)/10^-6)) Time, O(1) Space):**\n  - `low = 0.0`, `high = max consecutive distance`.\n  - Termination condition: Run while `high - low > 1e-6` (precision limit).\n  - Predicate function: For a trial max distance `dist`, count how many stations are needed across all intervals:\n    `stationsNeeded += (stations[i] - stations[i-1]) / dist`.\n  - If `stationsNeeded <= k`: Distance `mid` is achievable; search smaller distances (`high = mid`).\n  - Otherwise: `low = mid`.\n\n### 💻 Real-Valued Binary Search Blueprint\n```cpp\nint numberOfGasStationsRequired(long double dist, vector<int> &arr) {\n    int cnt = 0;\n    for (int i = 1; i < arr.size(); i++) {\n        int numberInBetween = (arr[i] - arr[i - 1]) / dist;\n        if ((arr[i] - arr[i - 1]) == numberInBetween * dist) {\n            numberInBetween--;\n        }\n        cnt += numberInBetween;\n    }\n    return cnt;\n}\n\nlong double minimiseMaxDistance(vector<int> &arr, int k) {\n    long double low = 0, high = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < arr.size() - 1; i++) {\n        high = max(high, (long double)(arr[i + 1] - arr[i]));\n    }\n    long double diff = 1e-6;\n    while (high - low > diff) {\n        long double mid = (low + high) / (2.0);\n        int cnt = numberOfGasStationsRequired(mid, arr);\n        if (cnt > k) {\n            low = mid;\n        } else {\n            high = mid;\n        }\n    }\n    return high;\n}\n```	take U forward (Striver)	https://www.youtube.com/@takeUforward	25	\N	\N	20	Easy	\N	1	[]	\N	\N	\N	\N
