ive design.", "isCorrect": false}], "question": "What is the Virtual DOM in React?", "explanation": "The Virtual DOM is a programming concept where an ideal, or 'virtual', representation of a UI is kept in memory and synced with the 'real' DOM by a library such as ReactDOM. This process is called reconciliation.", "correctAnswer": "C", "correct_index": 2, "correct_answer": "A lightweight copy of the real DOM kept in memory, used to determine the most efficient way to update the actual DOM."}, {"type": "multiple_choice", "answer": "B", "options": [{"text": "Java Server Extension, used for backend rendering.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "JavaScript XML, a syntax extension that allows writing HTML-like code within JavaScript.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "JSON Syntax Exchange, used for API communication.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "JavaScript XSS, a security feature.", "isCorrect": false}], "question": "What does JSX stand for and what is its role in React?", "explanation": "JSX produces React 'elements'. It describes what the UI should look like. It is not required to use React, but it is highly recommended because it makes the code more readable and easier to write.", "correctAnswer": "B", "correct_index": 1, "correct_answer": "JavaScript XML, a syntax extension that allows writing HTML-like code within JavaScript."}, {"type": "multiple_choice", "answer": "C", "options": [{"text": "npm create-react-app my-app", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "npx create-react-app my-app", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "npm create vite@latest my-app --template react", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "npm init react-app my-app", "isCorrect": false}], "question": "How do you create a React application using the Vite bundler?", "explanation": "Vite is a modern, fast build tool. `npm create vite@latest` initializes a new project, and you select the React template. Create React App (CRA) is no longer the recommended approach for new projects.", "correctAnswer": "C", "correct_index": 